tion of \"Integrated Security System\" before the \nterrorists attack at CST railway station in Mumbai on 26th November, \n2008; and \n(b) if so, the details thereof? \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS (SHRI R. VELU): (a) \nand (b) Installation of an Integrated Security System has been approved \nat all Railway Stations of four Metro cities of Chennai, Delhi, Kolkata \nand Mumbai (under Built On Operate Transfer (BOOT) model) and  \n†Original notice of the question was received in Hindi. \n\n308 \n140 other vulnerable / sensitive stations of Indian Railways (under \noutright purchase model). This system consists of the following four \nbroad areas:- \n1. Internet protocol based CCTV System. \n2. Access control. \n3. Personal and baggage screening system. \n4. Explosive detection and disposal system. \nGuidelines & technical specifications of equipment have been \ncirculated to the General Managers of Indian Railways for implementing \nthe project. \nProposals for new railway lines by Maharashtra \n673. SHRI Y.P. TRIVEDI: Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to \nstate: \n(a) the number of proposals for new railway lines submitted by the \nState of Maharashtra to his Ministry still pending for consideration; and \n(b) the present status of each project and by when each project is \nlikely to be cleared? \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS (SHRI R. VELU): (a) \nand (b) Details of proposals for new railway lines submitted by \nGovernment of Maharasthra alongwith their status are as under: \nSl.No. Proposals for new line submitted\n Status \n by Govt. of Maharashtra \n1 2  3 \n1. Satara-Pandharpur-Miraj& Baramati Survey not sanctioned. However, \n to Miraj New Line. Baramati-Lonand new line is  \n  sanctioned which would connect  \n  Baramati to Miraj. \n2. Manmad-Dhule-Shirpur-Indore Survey completed. However, survey  \n (3.50 km) & Manmad Sillod for Manmad-Sillod is not \nsanctioned. \n3. Pandharpur-Lonand Survey completed recently. \n4. Guhagar (Chiplun)-Lonand Survey not sanctioned. \n5. Jalna-Washim Survey not sanctioned. \n6. Shegaon-Jalna Survey not sanctioned. \n7. Manmad-Malegaon Survey completed in 2004-05. \nCould  \n  not be taken up due to \nunremunerative  \n\n309 \n  nature and constraint of \nresources. \n8. Pune-Nagar-Nashik Survey completed in 2000-01. \nCould  \n  not be taken up due to \nunremunerative  \n  nature and constraint of \nresources. \n9. Solapur-Tuljapur-Osmanabad Survey completed in 2004-05. \nCould  \n  not be taken up due to \nunremunerative  \n  nature and constraint of \nresources. \n\n310 \n1 2  3 \n10. Miraj-Kavthe Mahankal Jat-Vijapur Survey not sanctioned. \n Miraj -Tasgaon Vita-Phalton-Baramati \n11. Ghatnandur to Parli new line Survey not sanctioned. \n12. Kalyan to Malshej Ghat via Survey taken up. \n Ahmednagar \n13. Malkapur-Solapur Survey not sanctioned. \n14. Rotegaon-Puntamba Survey taken up. \n15. Kanakavli-Kolhapur Survey not sanctioned. \n16. Kolhapur-Ratnagiri Survey completed in 2000-01. \nCould  \n  not be taken up due to \nunremunerative  \n  nature and constraint of \nresources. \n17 Karad-Chiplum Survey taken up. \n18. Jalna-Khamgaon Survey completed in 2001-02. \nCould  \n  not be taken up due to \nunremunerative  \n  nature and constraint of \nresources. \n19. Dhule-Nardhana  Survey completed. \n20. Barshi-Beed-Jalna-Hingoli- Survey not sanctioned. However, \n Yavatmal-Wardha Wardha-Yavatmal-Pusad-Nanded  \n  included in the Budget 2008-09. \n It is not feasible to indicate time frame for clearance of all the \nprojects. \nPosts in group A, B, C and D \n674. SHRI PRASANTA CHATTERJEE: \n SHRI MOHAMMED AMIN: \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n(a) the number of existing posts in category A, B, C and D in his \nMinistry as on 30th June, 2008; \n(b) the number of posts abolished during the period 2004 to 2008, year \nand category-wise; and \n(c) the name of the services which have been out- sourced during last \nfive years? \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS (SHRI R. VELU): (a) \n\n311 \nThe number of existing posts in category A, B, C and D as on 30.6.2008 is \nas under: \nCategory A : 12367 \nCategory B : 6047 \nCategory C : 1021879 \nCategory D : 529163 \n\n312 \n(b)The number of posts abolished during the period 2004-2008, year and \ncategory-wise is as under: \nYear #                                                      Posts \nabolished \n Category 'A' Category 'B' \n2004 *679 499 \n2005 *203 *148 \n2006 *705 217 \n2007 *434 *235 \n2008 *140 17 \n(upto 30th June) \nYear $                                                     Posts \nabolished \n Category 'C' Category 'D' \n2004-05 *8439 28276 \n2005-06 1037 21673 \n2006-07 *7527 14540 \n2007-08 *7697 11788 \n2008 *1803 45 \n(upto 30th June) \n# year represents from January to December. \n$ year represents Financial Year. \n* sign shows increase. \n(c) The information is being collected and will be laid on the Table \nof the House. \nRenovation of railway stations in Delhi \n675. DR. V. MAITREYAN: Will the Minister of RAILWAYS pleased to state: \n(a) what is the total budget allocation for renovation and \nmodernization of railway stations in the capital; \n(b) whether they are running as per schedule for the Commonwealth \nGames 2010; \n(c) by when they are likely to be completed; \n(d) whether the projects are going on as per the scheduled time-frame; \nand \n(e) what would be the main advantage and facilities which would be \nprovided to the travelling public once they are renovated? \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS (SHRI R. VELU): (a) \nBudget allocation, during 2008- 09, of railway stations in the capital \n(Delhi area) for renovation and modernization is Rs. 2195 lakhs under \nPlan Head - Passenger Amenities. \n\n313 \n(b) to (d) Yes, Sir. Works in this regard at identified stations are \ngoing on as per schedule and are planned for completion during 2009-10. \n(e) On completion, passengers will have the benefits in the form of \nbetter facilities of A.C. waiting rooms, more sitting arrangements, \nalighting/boarding of trains, platform sheds, public conveniences, \npassenger dispersal system, better ambience and cleanliness, amenable \nplatforms depending upon category of stations. \n\n314 \nIncrease of berths in reserved coaches \n†676. SHRI RUDRA NARAYAN PANY: Will the Minister of  RAILWAYS be \npleased to state: \n(a) whether Government is aware of the fact that a result of increase \nin number of berths from 72 to 81 in reserve coaches, passengers are \nfacing great inconvenience; \n(b) whether complaints are received from passengers about the \ninconvenience caused due to this increase; \n(c) whether any complaint has been received by Government in this \nregard or Government is aware of the public discontentment; and \n(d) if so, the measures through which Government is considering to \nsolve this serious problem? \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS (SHRI R. VELU): (a) \nto (c) Yes, Sir. References from passengers about additional berths in \nthe Sleeper coaches mainly were of inconvenience and discomfort caused by \nincreased congestion and inadequate space. \n(d) The policy has been reviewed. It has now been decided to \ndiscontinue the scheme of provision of additional side middle berths in \nsleeper class coaches. Such berths provided in the already modified \ncoaches shall be gradually removed within a period of six months. \nFare concession to handicapped persons \n677. SHRIMATI HEMA MALINI: Will the Minister of  RAILWAYS be pleased to \nstate: \n(a) whether Government is aware that handicapped persons do not get \nrailway fare concessions in Rajdhani trains; and \n(b) if so, the reasons for not extending the concession in those \ntrains to handicapped persons? \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS (SHRI R. VELU): (a) \nYes, Sir. \n(b) Rajdhani trains are premium trains in which scope of concession \nhas been kept limited to patronize full fare paying passengers. \nEncroachment of railway land \n678. SHRI B.K. HARIPRASAD: Will the Minister of  RAILWAYS be pleased to \nstate: \n(a) whether for management of railway land, there are no separate land \n\n315 \nmanagement cells in most of the zones and divisions and the work is \nentrusted to officials with other duties who are not trained to function \nas Estate Officers to decide on the cases of encroachments; \n(b) whether Railways had given an assurance in Parliament in 1999 that \nthere would be no fresh encroachments on railway land and whether despite \nthis assurance more than 16,000 new encroachments have taken place; and \n†Original notice of the question was received in Hindi. \n\n316 \n(c) the reasons for a large number of pending cases under the Public \nPremises Eviction Act? \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS (SHRI R. VELU): (a) \nto (c) Information is being collected and will be laid on the Table of \nthe House. \nClassification of goods for freight determination \n†679. SHRI RAJ MOHINDER SINGH MAJITHA: \n SHRI SHIVANAND TIWARI: \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n(a) whether it is a fact that Railways have categorised goods under \ndifferent categories for the purpose of deciding freight fare and if so, \nthe total number of such categories existing during December, 2008; \n(b) the number of goods included recently in each category; and \n(c) the freight charges under each category? \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS (SHRI R. VELU): (a) \nYes, Sir. There are a total of 16 different categories for the \nclassification of goods including 4 low rated commodities. \n(b) Number of commodities included in each Class are given in Goods \nTariff No. 45 Part-I (Vol. II) as amended from time to time. \n(c) Distance based freight rates from 100 km to 3500 km. are given in \nthe Goods Tariff No. 44, Part-II, effective from 1.7.2006. \nClosure of printing presses of railway \n†680. MISS ANUSUIYA UIKEY: Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be \npleased to state: \n(a) whether it is a fact his Ministry has decided to close down \nRailways' printing presses which were running for last four decades; \n(b) if so, the reasons for closing down of printing presses; \n(c) the manner in which the stationery meant for Railways would get \nprinted in view of closure of printing presses; and \n(d) what is Railways' planning for rehabilitation of employees \nrendered unemployed as a result of closure of printing presses? \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS (SHRI R. VELU): (a) \nNo, Sir. It has been decided for partial merger of small presses with the \nmajor presses. \n(b) to (d) Do not arise. \nQuality of food supplied in trains \n\n317 \n681. SHRI KAMAL AKHTAR: \n SHRI NAND KISHORE YADAV: \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n†Original notice of the question was received in Hindi. \n\n318 \n(a) whether Government is aware that the quality of food supplied and \nthe quantity served thereof through trains passing through Uttar Pradesh \nand Kerala especially 2625/2626 Kerala Express, Rajdhani/Shatabdi are \ndeteriorating day by day after the private contractor's regime; \n(b) the details of the private contractors serving food in the Kerala \nExpress; \n(c) the details of specifications of food and the prices fixed by the \nRailways while grant in the contracts, item-wise; and \n(d) the mechanism to monitor the food quality/quantity in the above \ntrains by the Railways? \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS (SHRI R. VELU): (a) \nThe quality and quantity of food served in trains of Indian Railways \nincluding those running through Uttar Pradesh and Kerala, are monitored \nby Indian Railway Catering and Tourism Corporation (IRCTC). \n(b) M/s KMA Caterers is the present licensee of Kerala Express. \n(c) Details of food and prices thereof are given in the Statement (See \nbelow). \n(d) Monitoring of quality and quantity of food is done with the help \nof:- \n(i) Customer Satisfaction Survey through M/s IMRB International, \n(ii) Food Audit conducted by M/s. TUV SUD, \n(iii) Pasting of stickers indicating menu and tariff of food and \nbeverages, \n(iv) Conducting special drives, inspections and surprise checks, in \naddition to regular  \n  checks by IRCTC's Quality Control Professionals. \nStatement \nDetails of Food and Prices thereof \nItem Details of Menu Rates \n1  2 3  \nStandard Breakfast  Veg. cutlets-2nos-100gms.\n  \n(in casserole) 2 bread slice with -10 gms. butter in chiplet  \nVegetarian of total weight -70 gms. \n(a) Bread Butter Tomato ketchup sachet - 15 gms. Rs. 17.00 \n and Cutlet Salt and pepper \n(b) Idli and Vada Idli 4 nos.- 200 gms. \n  Urad Vada 4 nos. -120 gms. \n  Chutney (packaged separately)-50 gms. \n\n319 \n(c) Upma and Vada Upma-100 gms. \n  Urad Vada 4 nos.- 120 gms. \n  Chutney (packaged separately)-50 gms. \n(d) Pongal and Pongal - 200 gms. \n Vada Urad Vada 4 nos.-120 gms. \n  Chutney (packaged Separately) - 50 gms. \n\n320 \n1  2 3  \nNon -Vegetarian Omlette of 2 eggs-90 gms. Rs.20.00 \nBread Butter and Two bread slice with 10 gms butter in  \nOmlette chiplet of total weight 70 gm  \n  Tomato Ketchup in sachet - 15 gms. \n  Salt and Pepper \nStandard Rice Pulao or Jeera rice or plain rice of  Rs. 30.00 \nCasserole Meals fine quality -150 gms.  \nVegetarian Paratha (2 nos.) or Chapati (4 nos.) or  \n  Poories (5 nos.)-100 gms.  \n  Dal or Sambhar (thick consistency) -150 gms. \n  Mix veg (seasonal)- 100 gms. \n  Curd - 100 gms. or sweet - 40 gms. \n  Pickle in sachet -15 gms \n  Packaged drinking water in sealed glasses -250 ml. \nNon-Vegetarian Rice Pulao or Jeera rice or plain rice of fine Rs. \n35.00 \n  quality -150 gms.  \n  Paratha (2 nos.) or Chapati (4 nos.) or  \n  Poories (5 no.)-100 gms.  \n  Dal or Sambhar (thick consistency) -150 gms. \n  Two egg curry - 200 gms. \n  Curd - 100 gms. or sweet - 40 gms. \n  Pickle in sachet- 15 gms \n  Packaged drinking water in sealed glasses - 250 ml. \nModernisation of stations in Uttar Pradesh \n682. SHRI KAMAL AKHTAR: \n SHRI NAND KISHORE YADAV: \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n(a) whether Government is taking steps to modernize railway stations \nin Uttar Pradesh; \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n(c) the stations identified for the purpose, so far; and \n(d) the steps being taken to provide minimum facilities at railway \nstations? \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS (SHRI R. VELU): (a) \nto (c) In order to bring about perceptible improvement in the \"Touch and \nFeel\" items, 67 stations from the State of Uttar Pradesh have been \nselected for modernization which are as under: Achnera, Agra Cantt, Agra \nFort, Aligarh Jn., Allahabad Jn., Amethi, Ayodhya, Azamgarh, Badshah \nNagar, Bahraich, Ballia, Banda, Bareilly, Bareilly City, Basti, Belthra \nRoad, Chandauli, Chitrakutdham Karvi, Deoria Sadar, Dildarnagar, Etawah, \nFaizabad, Farukhabad, Fatehpur, Firozabad, Gazipur City, Ghaziabad, \nGonda, Gorakhpur, Hapur, Hardoi, Idgah, Jaunpur Jn., Jhansi, Kanpur \n\n321 \nCentral, Khalilabad, Khurja Jn., Kosikalan, Lakhimpur, Lalitpur, Lucknow \n(NR), Lucknow City, Lucknow Jn. (NER), Mahoba, Manduadih, Mathura, \nMathura Cantt., Mau Jn., Meerut City, Mirzapur, Moradabad, Mughal Sarai, \nNaini, Orai, Prayag, Rai- Bareilly, Raja ki Mandi, Rampur, Renukoot, \nSaharanpur, Salempur, Shahjahanpur, Sitapur, Sultanpur, Unnao, Varanasi \nand Vindhyachal. \n\n322 \n(d) Minimum essential amenities (MEA) at railway stations have already \nbeen provided. Further augmentation of passenger amenities at station \ncommensurate with increase in passenger traffic/earnings is a continuous \nprocess and is undertaken through Annual Works Programme depending upon \navailability of funds and other relative priorities. \nRailway projects in Uttar Pradesh \n683. SHRI KAMAL AKHTAR: \n SHRI NAND KISHORE YADAV: \n SHRI MOHAMMED ADEEB: \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n(a) the details of ongoing projects of Northern and North Eastern \nRailway in Uttar Pradesh; \n(b) the details of the projects which are likely to be completed in \ntime and those running behind schedule; \n(c) whether it is a fact that most of the works of NER are not \ncompleted in time; and \n(d) if so, the reasons therefor and the remedial measures taken \nthereon? \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS (SHRI R. VELU): (a) \nand (b) Details of ongoing projects of Northern/and North Eastern \nRailways in Uttar Pradesh are as under:- \nSl. Name of the work Length Railway Target date \nfor  \nNo.   (Km.)  completion  \n    wherever  \n    fixed. \n(earlier/ \n    revised) \n1 2 3 4 5 \nNew lines \n1. Deoband - Roorkee 27.45 Northern  \n2. Hathua-Bhatni 79.64 North Eastern 2008-09 \n3. Chhitauni-Tamkuhi Road 58.88 North Eastern \nDoublings \n1. Amroha-Kankather 31.00 Northern 07-08/08-09 \n2. Sahibabad Anand Vihar 3rd & 4th line 5.75 Northern\n 07-08/08-09 \n3. Hapur- Kankather 42.71 Northern 2008-09 \n\n323 \n4. Utratia-Zafrabad (balance part) 148.0 Northern 2010-11 \n5. Gonda-Manakpur 26.51 North Eastern \n6. Gorakhpur-Sajanwa 17.70 North Eastern 07-08/09-10 \n7. Babhnan-Manakpur 30.15 North Eastern 07-08/08-09 \n8. Sajanwa-Munderwa 32.19 North Eastern 2008-09 \n\n324 \n1 2 3 4 5 \n9. Munderwa-Babhnan 45.5 North Eastern 2008-09 \n10. Gorakhpur-Baitalpur 34.0 North Eastern 07-08/09-10 \n11. Barabanki-Burhwal 29.0 North Eastern \n12. Bhatni-Baitalpur 28.07 North Eastern \n13. Ghaghra Ghat - Chauk Ghat 5.63 North Eastern 07-08/09-10 \n14. Bhatni-Jiradei 38.11 North Eastern \n15. Mau-Indara 8.0 North Eastern \nGauge conversion \n1. Kanpur-Kasganj-Mathura  544.5 North Eastern 2008-09 \n and Kasganj- Bareilly-Lalkua \n2. Kaptanganj-Thawe-Siwan-Chhapra 233.5 North Eastern 2008-09 \n3. Aunrihar-Jaunpur 59.0 North Eastern 08-09/09-10 \n4. Gonda-Gorakhpur with Anand  81.28 North Eastern 2009-10 \n Nagar-Nautanwa \n5. Gonda-Bahraich-Sitapur-Lucknow  60.0 North Eastern \n Ph-I. \n6. Bhojipura-Tanakpur 101.79 North Eastern \n(c) and (d) All the works are progressed in phased manner as per \navailability of resources and keeping in view the quantum of work \ninvolved and constraints in completion of various works particularly \ndoubling which require non interlocked working. There have been delays in \nsome of the works due to failure of and delay in finalization of \ncontracts, delay in forestry clearance including tree cutting, abnormally \nheavy and prolonged rainfall, land acquisition by State Govt. and steep \nrise in steel and cement prices. Remedial measures have been taken by way \nof modification in contract conditions, empowerment of field units, \nproviding funds through internal generation and participation by State \nGovts. The matter has been taken up with S tate Governments for land \nacquisition and forestry clearance including tree cutting. \nElectrification of rail sections \n†684. SHRI KRISHAN LAL BALMIKI: Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be \npleased to state: \n(a) the details of the policy of his Ministry regarding \nelectrification of rail sections; \n\n325 \n(b) whether it is not appropriate that maximum number of rail sections \nbe electrified; and \n(c) the number of proposals sent by the State of Rajasthan for the \nelectrification of rail sections and the details of their present status? \n†Original notice of the question was received in Hindi. \n\n326 \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS (SHRI R. VELU): (a) \nand (b) Electrification projects are considered primarily on traffic \nvolumes, economic viability and operational necessity. \n(c) The State Government of Rajasthan had recommended electrification \nof Bina- Kota, Jaipur- Sawai Madhopur and Ratlam- Neemuch-Chittorgarh \nsections, amongst which, work is in progress on Bina-Kota section. \nDiversion of allocation for railway safety and security \n685. DR. K. MALAISAMY: Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to \nstate: \n(a) the potential areas still remaining to be tapped or exploited for \nincreasing the revenue and expenditure areas from which economy and \nsavings can be obtained; \n(b) whether it is a fact that the Budget allocation meant for railway \nsafety and security has been diverted to other purposes; and \n(c) if so, the details for the last three years? \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS (SHRI R. VELU): (a) \nRailways are making all out efforts to maximize its revenue from its core \nactivity of transportation of freight and passengers. In this direction, \nthroughput enhancement works have been taken up for removal of capacity \nconstraints in critical section for capturing more traffic. Number of \npassenger trains are being introduced and frequency of existing trains \nare also being increased in order to increase passenger earnings. \nBesides, railways are also exploring the avenues of revenue generation by \ncommercial exploitation of railway land not required for operational \npurposes especially in metro areas through development of commercial and \nresidential complexes and through advertisement at prominent locations on \nrailway land, trains and at stations. Additional revenue is also \nanticipated from setting up of Budget Hotels by Indian Railway Tourism \nand Catering Corporation (IRCTC). \nOn the expenditure side, railways are taking all possible measures for \neconomy and austerity in every area, with emphasis on better utilization \nof assets and rolling stock, improved maintenance practices through \nsuperior and latest technology, right sizing and increasing the \nefficiency of manpower etc. \n(b) and (c) No, Sir. Adequate funds are being provided for Safety and \nSecurity as per requirement. \nRail link between Chennai Egmore and Chennai Central Railway Stations \n686. DR. K. MALAISAMY: Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to \nstate: \n(a) whether the rail linkage between two gate- way of Tamil Nadu viz \n\n327 \nChennai Egmore railway station and Chennai Central railway junction was \nrightly conceived and foundation ceremony conducted during 2003 and then \nthe Government of Tamil Nadu promised to spare the requisite land; \n(b) if so, what is holding up proceeding further; and \n(c) whether there could be a categorical assurance as to when the \nproject could be taken up for execution and the time-frame for completion \nof the work in the wake of the long felt need of the people? \n\n328 \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS (SHRI R. VELU): (a) \nYes, Sir. \n(b) Tamil Nadu Government has not conveyed its clearance for the B.G. \nconnectivity between Chennai Central and Egmore as it would clash with \nthe alignments under the two major projects viz Chennai Metro Rail \nproject and the project of National Highways Authority of India (NHAI) to \nconstruct Elevated Expressway connecting Chennai port and Maduravoyal. \nFurther, the proposed rail link cannot be constructed without the \nflyover on EVR Periyar High Road for which there is no clearance \navailable from Tamil Nadu State Government side. The Government of Tamil \nNadu has been requested to review the decision and send its no objection \nfor execution of the project. Their response is awaited. \n(c) In view of status explained in (b) above no categorical assurance \ncan be given at this stage as to when the project can be taken for up \nexecution. \nAccidents at unmanned railway crossings \n†687. SHRI SHREEGOPAL VYAS: Will the Minister of  RAILWAYS be \npleased to state: \n(a) the number of collisions between vehicles similar to one that took \nplace between an engine and a bus on 2nd February, 2009 at Firozpur and \nthe number of passenger killed therein during last three years, zone-wise \nand State-wise; \n(b) the percentage of unmanned level crossings that would be changed \ninto manned level crossings in the Eleventh Five Year Plan; and \n(c) whether research is being done on remote sensing/signalling etc. \nto avoid such situations? \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS (SHRI R. VELU): (a) \nZone-wise number of unmanned level crossing accidents involving dashing \nof bus/van with trains and the number of persons killed and injured \ntherein during 2005-06, 2006-07 and 2007-08 and the current year 2008- 09 \nis as under:- \nYear Railway State Number of Number of Number \n   Accidents persons of \n    killed persons  \n     injured \n1 2 3 4 5 6 \n2005-06 South Western Karnataka 1 5 4 \n Northern Punjab 1 2 3 \n  Haryana 1 3 5 \nTotal   3 10 12 \n2006-07 North Western Rajasthan 1 5 12 \n West Central Rajasthan 1 0 9 \n\n329 \n Western Gujarat 1 6 12 \n Northern Punjab 1 3 23 \nTOTAL   4 14 56 \n†Original notice of the question was received in Hindi. \n\n330 \n1 2 3 4 5 6 \n2007-08 Southern Tamil Nadu 1 11 11 \n North Eastern Uttar Pradesh 1 3 9 \nTOTAL   2 14 20 \n2008-09 South East Maharashtra 1 0 6 \n(Upto Central \n13.02.09) Northern Punjab 1 3\n 13 \nTOTAL   2 3 19 \n(b) No such percentage is targeted. However, as on 01.01.2009, out of \napproximately 17,580 Nos. unmanned level crossings on Indian Railways, \n1286 Nos. qualify criteria for manning. All these are likely to be manned \nin next five years. \n(c) Trials to give audio visual warning to road users providing Train \nActuated Warning Device at gates have been done in recent past. But, \nthese trials have not been found successful. It has been decided recently \nto conduct experimental trials of radio based Gate Warning System on \nNorthern Railway. \nChange in name of Nanded station \n688. SARDAR TARLOCHAN SINGH: Will the Minister of  RAILWAYS be pleased \nto state: \n(a) whether the name of Nanded railway station in Maharashtra has been \nchanged as Hazoor Saheb Nanded; \n(b) if so, since when; and \n(c) if not, how long it would take? \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS (SHRI R. VELU): (a) \nto (c) Instructions have since been issued for renaming of 'Nanded' \nrailway station as 'Hazur Sahib Nanded' railway station. \nTicket booking service in rural areas \n†689. SHRI SAMAN PATHAK: Will the Minister of  RAILWAYS be \npleased to state: \n(a) whether Government has introduced railway ticket booking service \nin rural areas also; \n(b) if so, the details thereof; and \n(c) whether there is any provision under said scheme to provide \nagencies to the unemployed youths of rural areas? \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS (SHRI R. VELU): (a) \n\n331 \nand (b) Yes, Sir. A scheme to appoint Gramin Ticket Booking Sewaks \n(GTBSs) at roadside stations excluding contractor- operated halts, where \nthe ticket booking arrangements was not satisfactory, was launched on \nEast Central Railway in the year 2006. At present, the scheme of GTBS is \noperative at 13 stations only. \n†Original notice of the question was received in Hindi. \n\n332 \n(c) The scheme provides the opportunity to unemployed youths to get \nagency for selling unreserved tickets. However, there is no specific \nquota in the scheme for unemployed youths. \nElectrification of New Jalpaiguri railway line \n†690. SHRI SAMAN PATHAK: Will the Minister of  RAILWAYS be \npleased to state: \n(a) whether Government is contemplating to electrify the New \nJalpaiguri railway line; \n(b) if so, the details thereof; and \n(c) by when the work on this project is likely to be started and \ncompleted? \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS (SHRI R. VELU): (a) \nto (c) New Jalpaiguri railway station falls on Barauni- Katihar-Guwahati \nrail line. Electrification of Barauni- Katihar-Guwahati section has been \nsanctioned at a cost of Rs.821.53 crore. Electrification work has been \nstarted in Barauni-Katihar section from January 2009. The entire section \nis targeted for completion by March, 2012. \nRail accident at unmanned crossing near Moga in Punjab \n691. SHRI VARINDER SINGH BAJWA: Will the Minister of  RAILWAYS be \npleased to state: \n(a) whether it is a fact that a school bus with school children \ntravelling therein met with an accident with a rail engine on an unmanned \ncrossing near Moga in Punjab, recently; \n(b) if so, the number of children who lost their lives and those \nseriously injured in the mishap; and \n(c) the extent of ex- gratia payment made by the Railways, if any, to \nthe parents of the children killed and injured? \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS (SHRI R. VELU): (a) \nand (b) Yes, Sir. On 02.02.2009 at 08.20 hours, one school van dashed \nagainst Diesel Light Engine at Unmanned Level Crossing No. 71- C between \nFirozeshah-Talwandi stations near Moga on Firozepur Division of Northern \nRailway. This accident resulted into death of 3 children, grievous \ninjuries to 6 children and simple injuries to 7 children. \n(c) As the accident at the unmanned level crossing near Moga has \nhappened due to carelessness of the Bus driver, no ex -gratia has been \npaid to the parents of those dead and injured children. \nRail-road over/under bridges in Himachal Pradesh \n692. SHRIMATI VIPLOVE THAKUR: Will the Minister of  RAILWAYS be pleased \n\n333 \nto state: \n(a) the details of proposed rail- road over/under bridges in Himachal \nPradesh pending for sanction; and \n(b) the time by when these projects are likely to be sanctioned and \nthe details of the funds allocated for these projects? \n†Original notice of the question was received in Hindi. \n\n334 \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS (SHRI R. VELU): (a) \nNo proposal is pending for Cost Sharing work, however, 3 proposals of \nROBs (Road Over Bridges) (I) near Fared on Pathankot- Jogindernagar \nSection (2) near Tillha Village on Sirhind- Unna Section and (3) near \nBaijnath Mahakal on Pathankot-Jogindernagar Section, are pending. \n(b) All the Three proposals are to be taken up on deposit terms. These \nwill be taken up only after State Govt. fulfills all the preliminary pre-\nrequisites & deposits money (Cost of the works) with Railways. \nMulti pronged programme to combat terrorism \n693. SHRI RAMDAS AGARWAL: \n SHRI DARA SINGH: \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n(a) what is the latest multi -pronged programme chalked out by Indian \nRailways to combat the menace of terrorist, naxalites and other \ndisruptive forces trying to target trains and stations; \n(b) the details thereof, till-date; \n(c) whether CCTVs have been installed at all metro and other railway \nstations as well as deployment of adequate number of RPF; and \n(d) what budgetary allocation has been made during the current \nfinancial year as compared to previous year? \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS (SHRI R. VELU): (a) \nto (c) Railway Protection Force, an Armed Force of the Union under \nMinistry of Railways, is presently supplementing the efforts of the \nrespective State Governments in combating terrorist, naxalites and other \ndisruptive activities over Railways. Although the maintenance of the law \nand order and to tackle the problem of terrorists, naxalites attacks and \nother disruptive activities over Railways is the responsibility of the \nState Government concerned through Government Railway Police. However, \nRailway Protection Force is supplementing the Government Railway Police \nto tackle such problems. Following measures have been initiated for \nstrengthening of RPF viz.- \ni) RPF/RPSF staff have been deployed at important stations and in trains \nand briefed to be prepared to tackle any situation. \nii) Staffs have been put on alert to prevent such incidents. \niii) Government Railway Police and State Police have also been asked to \nstrengthen the security arrangements at Railway stations and in \n\n335 \ntrains. \niv) Close coordination with State Police and Intelligence agencies \nhave been maintained to share information of such acts. \nv) Allocation of Rs 60.76 Crore for procurement of modern security \nequipment for RPF. \nvi) Allocation of Rs 14.26 Crore for procurement of vehicles for RPF. \n\n336 \nvii) Implementation of an Integrated Security System over all the \nrailway stations of four metro cities viz. Delhi, Mumbai, Kolkata & \nChennai and 140 other sensitive/vulnerable railway stations of the \ncountry. The above system consists of following four broad areas- \n1) IP based CCTV surveillance system. \n2) Access Control \n3) Personal and Baggage Screening System and \n4) Bomb Detection and Disposal System \nviii) RPF has been upgraded with modern weaponry/security gadgets like \nINSAS 5.56mm rifles, AK- 47, SLR 7.62mm, Carbine 9 mm, Pistol 9mm, \nBullet Proof Jackets and Helmets, Walkie- Talkie, Hand Held Metal \nDetectors, Door Frame Metal Detectors, etc. \n(ix) It has been proposed to give commando training to 2 RPSF Battalions \nand deployment of trained staff at strategic locations. It has also \nbeen proposed to raise three additional Battalions of RPSF. \n(d) There is no separate Head for Security purposes. Funds are made \navailable for the procurement of Security equipments and \nmodernization/strengthening of the Railway Protection Force from \nappropriate heads of account like Works Programme, Machinery & Plants \n(M&P) Head, Passenger Amenity Head etc. Allocation of funds for Security \npurposes is made as per requirement. \nProposals for railway projects in Maharashtra \n694. SHRI SHARAD ANANTRAO JOSHI: Will the Minister of  RAILWAYS be \npleased to state: \n(a) whether proposals/references have been received from the State of \nMaharashtra from time to time for making adequate provision in railway \nbudget for new railway line, widening of existing railway lines and \ndoubling of existing railway lines in Maharashtra on the demand and \nrecommendations of railway project by MPs, MLAs and MLCs; and \n(b) if so, the details thereof and the action taken in this regard \nwith particular reference to attachment of Nanded railway division to \nCentral Railway and transfer of railway land under the abandoned Lature-\nHarangul narrow gauge railway line to the Government of Maharashtra? \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS (SHRI R. VELU): (a) \nand (b) Yes, Sir. References have been received from State Government for \nproviding sufficient fund for early completion of projects. As regards \n\n337 \ntransfer of railway lan d under the abandoned Latur-  Harangul narrow \ngauge, railway land measuring 30.36 hect. out of 39.56 hect. land has \nsince been handed over to Government of Maharashtra. \nThere is no proposal under consideration to attach Nanded Railway \nDivision with Central Railway. Moreover, the decision to place a \nparticular division under a particular zone is taken based on the \noperational administrative requirements without any regional \nconsideration. The present arrangement is working satisfactorily. \n\n338 \nStrategy to tackle fog \n695. MS. MABEL REBELLO: \n SHRI B.J. PANDA: \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n(a) whether Railways have worked out some strategy to tackle fog with \nnight vision goggles for drivers of the running trains; \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n(c) whether a GPS device was developed by the Railways to fight fog; \nand \n(d) if so, how far has it proved successful to address the fog issue? \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS (SHRI R. VELU): (a) \nNo, Sir. \n(b) Does not arise. \n(c) and (d) Some trials with GPS (Global Positioning System) to combat \nthe fog are being undertaken. However, it would be too premature to \ncomment on the performance of this equipment as to how it would be \nhelpful for working of trains in foggy weather. \nTrains without pantry car facilities \n696. SHRI T.T.V. DHINAKARAN: Will the Minister of  RAILWAYS be pleased \nto state: \n(a) the list of long distance trains not having pantry car facilities; \n(b) the reasons for not providing pantry car facilities in those \ntrains; and \n(c) the time by when pantry car facilities would be provided? \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS (SHRI R. VELU): (a) \nA Statement is attached (See below). \n(b) and (c) Attachment of pantry cars to trains is based on various \nconsiderations such as priority of the train, journey time, commercial \njustification and availability of pantry cars, etc. No time- frame for \nattachment of pantry cars to all the long distance trains, can be given. \nStatement \nList of long distance Mail/Express trains (journey time of more than 24 \nhours  \nin both ways) running without Pantry Car \nS.No.            Train No.     Train Name \n1                 2           3 \n\n339 \n1 1039 1040 Sri Chattrapati Sahu Maharaj (T) - Gondia \nMaharashtra  \n   Express \n2 1043 1044 Lokmanaya Tilak (T) - Madurai Express \n3 1053 1054 Nizamuddin - Sri Chatrapati Sahu Maharaj (T) \nExpress \n4 1055 1056 Gorakhpur-Lokmanaya Tilak (T) Godan  Express \n\n340 \n1                 2           3 \n5 1057 1058 Dadar-Amritsar Exp. \n6 1059 1060 Chhapra - Lokmanaya Tilak (T) Godan Express \n7 1067 1068 Lokmanaya Tilak (T) - Faizabad Saket Express \n8 1069 1070 Lokmanaya Tilak (T) - Allahabad Exp \n9 1071 1072 Lokmanaya Tilak (T) - Varanasi Kamayani Express \n10 1093 1094 Mumbai - Varanasi Mahanagari Express \n11 1123 1124 Barauni-Gwaiior Mail \n12 1159 1160 Howrah - Gwalior Chambal Express \n13 1181 1182 Howrah - Agra Cantt Chambal Express \n14 1405 1406 Manmad - Visakapatnam/Kakinada Town Express \n15 1447 1448 Howrah - Jabalpur Shaktipunj Express \n16 1463 1464 Veeraval - Jabalpur Express \n17 1465 1466 Veeraval - Jabalpur Express \n18 2145 2146 Lokmanya Tilak (T) Bhubaneswar Exp. \n19 2315 2316 Sealdah-Ajmer Ananaya Exp. \n20 2317 2318 Sealdah-Amritsar Akal Takht Exp. \n21 2327 2328 Howrah-Dehradun Upasana Exp. \n22 2405 2406 Bhusawal - Nizamuddin Gondwana Exp. \n23 2409 2410 Bilaspur-Nizamuddin Gondwana Exp. \n24 2645 2646 Ernakulam-Nizamuddin Millenium Exp. \n25 2647 2648 Coimbatore-Nizamuddin Kongu Exp. \n26 2941 2942 Asansol-Ahmedabad Parasnath Exp. \n27 2977 2978 Ernakulam- Jaipur Marusagar Exp. \n28 3009 3010 Howrah - Dehradun Doon Express \n29 3019 3020 Howrah-Kathgodam Bagh Exp. \n30 3025 3026 Howrah - Bhopal Express \n31 3039 3040 Howrah - Delhi Janata Exp. \n32 3049 3050 Howrah- Arnritsar Exp. \n33 3111 3112 Sealdah - Delhi Lal Quila Express \n34 3133 3134 Sealdah -Varanasi Express \n35 3287 3288 Tata Nagar/Durg - Patna South Bihar Express \n\n341 \n1                 2           3 \n36 3289 3290 Rajendranagar-Jammu Tawi Archana Exp. \n37 3307 3308 Dhanbad - Firozpur Ganga Sutlej Express \n38 3447 3448 Bhagalpur - Dadar Express \n39 4007 4008 Muzaffarpur-Delhi Sadhbhavana Exp. \n40 4015 4016 Raxaul - Delhi Sadbhavana Express \n41 4017 4018 Muzaffarpur- Delhi Sadbhavana Express \n42 4265 4266 Varanasi-Dehradun Exp. \n43 4309 4310 Ujjain - Dehradun Ujjaini Express \n44 4311 4312 Bareilly Bhuj Ala Hazrat Express \n45 4313 4314 Dadar - Bareilly Express \n46 4317 4318 Indore - Dehradun Express \n47 4523 4524 Muzaffarpur - Ambala Cantt Harihar Express \n48 4649 4650 Darbhanga - Amritsar Saryu Yamuna Express \n49 4673 4674 Darbhanga - Amritsar Shaheed Express \n50 4707 4708 Bikaner - Bandra (T) Ranakpur Express \n51 4853 4854 Varanasi-Jodhpur Marudhar Exp. \n52 5001 5002 Muzaffarpur - Dehradun Express \n53 5017 5018 Lokmanya Tilak(T) -Gorakhpur Kashi Exp. \n54 5159 5160 Durg - Chhapra Samath Express \n55 5209 5210 Barauni - Amritsar Jan Sewa Express \n56 5211 5212 Darbhanga - Amritsar Jan Nayak Express \n57 5267 5268 Muzaffarpur-Lokmanya Tilak(T) Jan Sadharan Exp. \n58 5269 5270 Muzaffarpur-Ahmedabad Jan Sadharan Exp. \n59 5707 5708 Katihar-Amritsar Exp. \n60 6003 6004 Howrah - Chennai Mail \n61 6031 6032 Chennai-Jammu Tawi Andaman Exp. \n62 6093 6094 Chennai - Lucknow Exp. \n63 6357 6358 Nagercoil-Howrah Gurudev Exp. \n64 6511 6512 Yashwantpur - Bilaspur Wain Ganga Express \n65 6525 6526 Kanyakumari - Bangalore Express \n66 6529 6530 Mumbai - Banagalore Udyan Express \n\n342 \n1                 2           3 \n67 6593 5594 Nanded - Bangalore Express \n68 6613 5614 Rajkot-Coimbatore Exp. \n69 7045 7046 Howrah - Hyderabad East Coast Express \n70 7479 7480 Puri-Tirupati Exp. \n71 7481 7482 Bilaspur - Tirupati Exp. \n72 8029 8030 Howrah-Lokmanya Tilak (T) Exp. \n73 8103 8104 Tata-Amritsar Jalliawalan Bagh Express \n74 8201 8202 Durg - Gorakhpur Express \n75 8233 8234 Indore - Bilaspur Narmada Express \n76 8415 8416 Bhubneshwar - Yeshwantpur Express \n77 8609 8610 Ranchi-Lokmanya Tilak (T) Exp. \n78 9019 9020 Bandra (T)-Dehradun Exp. \n79 9023 9024 Mumbai Central -Firozpur Janata Exp. \n80 9049 9050 Bandra (T) - Patna Express \n81 9111 9112 Ahmedabad - Jammu Tawi Express \n82 9165 9166 Ahmedabad-Darbhanga Sabarmati Exp. \n83 9167 9168 Ahmedabad-Varanasi Sabarmati Exp \n84 9265 9266 Okha - Dehradun Uttaranchal Express \n85 9305 9306 Indore - Howrah Shipra Express \n86 9321 9322 Indore - Rajendranagar Express \n87 9569 9570 Okha-Varanasi Exp. \nShortage of coolies at stations in Delhi \n697. SHRI RAJEEV CHANDRASEKHAR: Will the Minister of  RAILWAYS be \npleased to state: \n(a) whether it is a fact that there is an acute shortage of coolies at \nall the major stations in Delhi which causes hardship to passengers \nparticularly the elderly and women and that it also leads to exploitation \nby the available coolies; \n(b) if so, the reasons for the shortage; \n(c) the approved and actual strength of coolies as on 1 st February, \n2009 at each of the stations; and \n\n343 \n(d) the steps proposed to ensure adequate number of coolies at each \nstation and also to ensure that they do not indulge in overcharging? \n\n344 \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS (SHRI R. VELU): (a) \nto (d) The appointment of Gangmen from among the licensed porters has led \nto the shortage at the stations of Delhi. The process of engagement of \nfresh licensed porters to overcome the shortage could not be initiated as \na large number of these newly appointed gangmen have submitted \nrepresentations for restoring their badges to work again as licensed \nporters. The sanctioned and existing strength of licensed porters at \nmajor stations of Delhi is as under: \nName of stations Sanctioned strength Existing strength \nNew Delhi 1407 648 \nDelhi Main 830 247 \nHazrat Nizammudin 431 316 \nDelhi Sarai Rohilla  25 16 \nTo ensure availability of licensed porters, redeployment of licensed \nporters within the division is being resorted to till such time the \nprocess of engaging fresh licensed porters could be initiated. The \nrequirement of licensed porters at Delhi main station is being reviewed \nand rationalized so that the surplus could be redeployed at New Delhi \nwhere there is major shortage. To overcome the problem of overcharging \nand exploitation by licensed porters, regular checks are being conducted \nat these stations. The badges of licensed porters involved in such \nactivities are being impounded/suspended. \nGrabbing of railway's land \n698. SHRI RAJEEV CHANDRASEKHAR: Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be \npleased to state: \n(a) the number of cases with area of land and structure belonging to \nRailways in Karnataka under adverse possession as on 1st January, 2009; \n(b) the action taken, so far, in each case to have the same \nvacated/restored; \n(c) whether the involvement of railway officials in land grabbing has \nbeen investigated; and \n(d) if so, the details thereof and the action taken against those \ninvolved? \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS (SHRI R. VELU): (a) \nState-wise details of encroachments on railway land are not maintained. \nThe State of Karnataka is covered by four zonal Railways, namely Central, \nSouthern, South Central and South Western Railways. There are 40331 \nnumber of encroachments covering area of 181.44 hectare as per details \ngiven below. \n\n345 \nRailway Zone Number Area (Hectare) \nCentral 27352 74 \nSouthern 9709 64.8 \nSouth Central 2728 26.27 \nSouth Western 542 16.37 \nTOTAL : 40331 181.44 \n\n346 \n(b) Railways are engaged in a continuous exercise to free their land \nof encroachments as per provisions contained in the Public Premises \n(Eviction of Unauthorised Occupants) Act, 1971 and Railways Act, 1989. \n(c) and (d) Involvement of railway officials in land grabbing has not \nbeen established or reported so far. \nReplacement of old rail tracks in Tamil Nadu \n699. SHRI B.S. GNANADESIKAN: Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased \nto state: \n(a) whether Government is aware that there is a need to evaluate and \nassess the strength of rail tracks between Madurai and Dindigul and \nMadurai and Virudhunagar since these rail tracks are many decade old; \n(b) if so, whether Government proposed to replace those weak rail \ntracks laid many decades ago leading possibilities for any mishap in \nthose railway lines of Tamil Nadu; \n(c) if so, the details thereof; and \n(d) if not, the reasons therefor? \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS (SHRI R. VELU): (a) \nYes, Sir. Regular assessment for strengthening of rail tracks between \nMadurai and Dindigul and Madurai and Virudhunagar are being done and \naction being taken on priority basis. \n(b) Replacement of rails is being planned as per requirement in phased \nmanner. \n(c) In Madurai- Dindigul section, about 28 km of rails have been \nreplaced during the current year and further replacement of rails is in \nprogress. In Madurai- Virudhunagar section also rail renewal is in \nprogress. \n(d) Does not arise. \nRevision of railway freight \n700. SHRI TAPAN KUMAR SEN: Will the Minister of  RAILWAYS be pleased to \nstate: \n(a) whether it is a fact that on and from February 1, 2009 \nclassifications of chemical manures, foodgrains, flours and pulses have \nbeen revised for the purpose of revision of railway freight; \n(b) if so, the details thereof; and \n(c) why such increase in freight has been announced through \n\n347 \nadministrative order on the eve of placement of Railway budget? \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS (SHRI R. VELU): (a) \nand (b) Yes, Sir. The Classification of Main Commodity Head 'Chemical \nManures' and 'Foodgrains, Flours and Pulses' has been revised from Class-\n120 to Class-130.  \n(c) Revision of freight rates is an ongoing exercise and is being done \nthroughout the year as and when required. \n\n348 \nIntroduction of trains \n†701. SHRI AVTAR SINGH KARIMPURI: Will the Minister of  RAILWAYS \nbe pleased to state: \n(a) the details of total number of new trains introduced in the year \n2007-08; and \n(b) out of these the details of total number of trains introduced for \nthe State of Punjab? \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAY S (SHRI R. VELU): (a) \nDuring the year 2007- 08, the following new trains were introduced over \nIndian Railways:- \n(Trains in Single) \n Mail/ Garib Passenger Mainline  Diesel  Jan  Sub \n Express Rath  Electric Electirc Shatabdi urban \n    Multiple  Multiple  \n    units Units  \n 94 14 84 6 10 2 162 \n(b) 1 pair of Express train between Amritsar and Indore has been \nintroduced during the year 2007-08 to serve the passengers of Punjab. \nExtra berths in coaches \n702. SHRI KALRAJ MISHRA: Will the Minister of  RAILWAYS be pleased to \nstate: \n(a) whether Government has decided to drop and reverse the proposal to \nadd extra berths in the AC- 3 tier and sleeper class in long distance \ntrains in view of complaints of inconvenience from the passengers \nconcerned; \n(b) if so, the loss incurred by the Railways in the process of \ncreating and dismantling of the added seats and in which trains and how \nmany additional berths/seats would have to be dismantled; and \n(c) the alternate steps contemplated to achieve the objective of \nshortening the waiting list and to cut down refunds? \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS (SHRI R. VELU): (a) \nand (b) Yes, Sir. The policy has been reviewed and it has now been \ndecided to discontinue the scheme of provision of additional side middle \nberths in sleeper and AC 3 Tier coaches. Such berths, wherever provided \nin the coaches, shall be gradually removed within a period of six months. \nIn the mean time, such coaches will be utilized in trains where the \n\n349 \njourney may not involve more than one night. \nThe scheme was introduced about 1.5 years back and such coaches have \nbeen progressively inducted in train services since then, thereby \nproviding more reserved accommodation to passengers and, though a \nsubsidiary benefit, leading to enhanced earnings as well. The removal of \nsuch berths shall also be done gradually and therefore, marginal losses, \nthat may happen, can not be estimated at this stage. An estimated 52030 \nside middle berths shall be required to be dismantled. \n†Original notice of the question was received in Hindi. \n\n350 \n(c) Following steps have been taken by the Railways to shortening the \nwaiting lists and to cut down refunds: \n(i) Developing additional seating capacity in trains by introducing \nnew regular trains. \n(ii) Running special trains during rush periods such as vacations, \nfestivals and important events etc. \n(iii) Enhancing the load of well patronized trains to the maximum to \nmeet the demand. \n(iv) Attaching additional coaches in trains to clear waiting list. \nNew railway line between Guwahati and Jogihopa \n703. KUMAR DEEPAK DAS: Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to \nstate: \n(a) whether Government is aware that there is long standing demand for \nthe construction of new railway line between Guwahati and Jogihopa via \nBarpeta-Hajo-Sualkuchi; \n(b) whether Government would consider the survey of such a railway \nline within current financial year in the greater interest of development \nof tourism and economy; and \n(c) if not, the reasons therefor? \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS (SHRI R. VELU): (a) \nAvailable records do not indicate such demand. \n(b) No, Sir. \n(c) Does not arise. \nUpgradation of Nagpur station \n704. SHRI VIJAY JAWAHARLAL DARDA: \n SHRI GIREESH KUMAR SANGHI: \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n(a) whether it is a fact that a recent study of Nagpur railway station \nhas opined construction of at least five more platforms at that station \nto cope up with the increasing load; \n(b) if so, whether upgradation of Nagpur station to world class would \nensure that five more, i.e. a total of 12 platforms would be available; \nand \n(c) whether request of the Federation of Investors, Traders and \nIndustries, to start new trains from Nagpur be implemented during 2008-\n\n351 \n09? \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS (SHRI R. VELU): (a) \nNo, Sir. No study of Nagpur station has been conducted by the Railways. \n(b) Nagpur has been identified as one of the 26 Railway stations \nproposed for development into World Class Stations. As far as the number \nof platforms is concerned, it is difficult to indicate the same as \nfeasibility study has not yet been commissioned. \n(c) Based on Public demand the following trains have been introduced \nwhich will serve Nagpur: \n\n352 \nNew Trains introduced: \nSl.No. Train No. From To Type Frequency\n Date \n1. 2135/2136 Pune Nagpur Garib Tri- 19.01.2009 \n    Rath weekly \n2. 4259/4260 Varanasi Rameshwaram Express Weekly Upto Chennai  \n      from 8.2.09 \n3. 2849/2850 Bilaspur Pune Express Weekly 3.7.08 \n4. 2119/2120 Amravati Nagpur Express 5 days 8.9.08 \nFollowing trains have also been announced in Railway Budget 2008- 09 (To \ncommence shortly): \nSl.No. Train No. From To Type Frequency \n1. 2879/2880 Bhubaneshwar Lokmanya Express Bi-weekly \n   Tilak (T) \n2. 2389/2390 Gaya Chennai Express weekly \nExtension: \nSl.No Train No. From To Type Upto Date of  \n      extension \n1. 2855/2856 Nagpur Raipur Express Bilaspur 1.7.2008 \n2. 2409/2410 Nizamuddin Bilaspur Gondwana Raigarh 25.2.2008 \n    Express \n3. 2139/2140 Nagpur Dadar (T) Sewagram Mumbai 14.12.08 \n    Express CST \nFrequency: \nSl.No. Train No. From To Type From To Date \nof  \n       increasing \n1 2151/2152 Lokmanya Howrah Samrasta 1 2 29.1.2009 \n  Tilak (T)  Express \nIncrease in diseases \n†705. SHRI PYARELAL KHANDELWAL: Will the Minister of  HEALTH AND \nFAMILY WELFARE be pleased to state: \n(a) whether there is a sharp rise in the serious diseases like cancer, \ndiabetes and heart disease etc. in the country during the last three \nyears; and \n(b) if so, the details of patients for the last three years, disease-\n\n353 \nwise and State-wise? \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE \n(SHRIMATI PANABAKA LAKSHMI) : (a) and (b) Health being a state subject, \nsuch information/data is not  \n†Original notice of the question was received in Hindi. \n\n354 \ncentrally maintained. The data available from National Cancer Registry \nProgramme of ICMR does indicate rise in the cancer cases in India. There \nare about nine lakh new Cancer patients occurring every year in the \ncountry. The diabetes and heart diseases are also increasing in the \ncountry. \nDrip and sprinkler irrigation \n706. SHRI R.C. SINGH: Will the Minister of AGRICULTURE be pleased to \nstate: \n(a) whether it is a fact that drip and sprinkler irrigation is rapidly \ngaining ground in country; \n(b) the number of hectares, district- wise, covered under drip \nirrigation in the State of West Bengal; and \n(c) the details of Central subsidy provided to farmers who are doing \ndrip irrigation in the State of West Bengal in the last three years; \nyear-wise? \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE (SHRI KANTILAL \nBHURIA): (a) Yes, Sir. \n(b) The district wise area covered under drip irrigation in the State \nof West Bengal is as under: \nSl.No. District Area covered under drip (ha) \n1. Burdwan 21 \n2. Malda 12 \n3. Paschim Midnapore 22 \n4. South 24 Parganas 0.6 \n TOTAL : 55.60 \n(c) The Central subsidy of Rs.195.67 lakh was released to eighteen \ndistricts of West Bengal during 2006- 07 under the Centrally Sponsored \nScheme on Micro Irrigation. Since, the subsidy released to the State was \nnot utilized fully, further release of funds could not be made. The \ndistrict wise details of central subsidy provided is given in the \nStatement. \nStatement \nDetails of district-wise release of funds during 2006-07 \nSl.No. Name of the District Funds released  \n  (Rs. in lakh) \n1 2 3  \n\n355 \n1. Bankura 13.37 \n2. Burdwan 8.63 \n3. Birbhum 8.50 \n4. Cooch Behar 7.74 \n5. Dakshin Dinajpur 6.38 \n\n356 \n1 2 3 \n6. Darjeeling 14.85 \n7. Hooghly 13.22 \n8. Howrah 9.41 \n9. Jalpaiguri 11.25 \n10. Malda 8.63 \n11. Murshidabad 8.63 \n12. Nadia 14.99 \n13. North 24 Parganas 11.24 \n14. Paschim Midnapore 10.99 \n15. Purba Midnapore 7.78 \n16. Purulia 20.53 \n17. South 24 Parganas 13.15 \n18. Uttar Dinajpur 6.38 \n TOTAL : 195.67 \n__________ \n12.00 NOON \n[MR. DEPUTY CHAIRMAN in the Chair.] \nSTATEMENT BY MINISTER CORRECTING ANSWER TO QUESTION \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE \n(SHRIMATI PANABAKA LAKSHMI): Sir, I lay on the Table a copy each (in \nEnglish and Hindi) of the statement correcting the answer to Unstarred \nQuestion 70 given in the Rajya Sabha on the 17th October, 2008 regarding \nchild and maternal mortality rates. \n__________ \nPAPERS LAID ON THE TABLE \nReport (2008-09) and Accounts (2007-08) of ICAR, New Delhi and related \npapers. \nTHE MINISTER OF AGRICULTURE AND THE MINISTER OF CONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD \nAND PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION (SHRI SHARAD PAWAR): Sir, I lay on the Table, a \ncopy each (in English and Hindi) of the following papers: \n (a) Annual Report of the Indian Council of Agricultural Research \n(ICAR), New Delhi, for the year 2008-2009. \n (b) Annual Accounts of the Indian Council of Agricultural Research \n(ICAR), New Delhi, for the year 2007- 2008, together with Audit \n\n357 \nReport thereon. \n (c) Sta