ioned at II above. [Placed in Library. See \nNo. L.T. 10600/09] \nII. A copy (in English and Hindi) of the Statement giving reasons for \nnot laying the Annual Report* of the National Institute of \nPharmaceutical Education and Research (NIPER), S.A.S. Nagar (Mohali), \nfor the year 2007-2008. [Placed in Library. See No. L.T. 10605/09] \n I. Notifications of the Ministry of Health and Family Welfare \n II. Report and Accounts (2007- 08) of various \ncouncils/Institutions/Fund and related papers \n THE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE \n(SHRIMATI PANABAKA LAKSHMI): Sir, I lay on the Table:- \nI. (i) A copy each (in English and Hindi) of the following Notifications \nof the Ministry of Health and Family Welfare (Department of \nHealth), under section 38 of the Drugs and Cosmetics Act, 1940: \n  (1) G.S.R. 780 (E), dated the 10th November, 2008, publishing \nthe Drugs and Cosmetics (Third Amendment) Rules, 2008. \n  (2) G.S.R. 46 (E), dated the 22nd January, 2009, publishing the \n\n360 \nDrugs and Cosmetics (First Amendment) Rules, 2009. \n  (3) G.S.R. 755 (E), dated the 27th October, 2008, publishing the \nDrugs and Cosmetics (Second Amendment) Rules, 2008, along \nwith delay statement. [Placed in Library. For (1) to (3) See \nNo. L.T. 10530/09] \n (ii) A copy (in English and Hindi) of the Ministry of Health and \nFamily Welfare (Department of Health and Family Welfare) \nNotification No. S.O. 2678 (E), dated the 18th November, 2008, \nappointing the 18th day of November, 2008, as the day on which \nthe provisions of Sections 16 to 18 (both inclusive), 81, 82, 83, \n84, 85, 86, 92 and 93), shall come into force under section 93 of \nthe Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. [Placed in Library. See \nNo. L.T. 10531/09] \n* The Annual Report of the National Institute of Pharmaceutical Education and \nResearch (NIPER), S.A.S. Nagar (Mohali) was laid on the Table on the 13th February, \n2009. \n\n361 \nII. A copy each (in English and Hindi) o