ै। \nमेरा आपसे �नवेदन यह� है �क आप वहां के �लए नए इंजन द�, िजससे आपका जो है �रटे ज क� बात है \nया यूनेस्को क� बात है, वह ठ�क लगे। इससे लोग� को लगेगा �क हमार� यह एक सच्ची है �रटे ज लाइन \nहै और जो सुचारू रूप से ठ�क चल रह� है। \nमहोदय, एक बात म� और कहना चाहूंगी �क हमार� जो पठानकोट-जो�गन्दर नगर लाइन है, इ स के \n�लए हमार� बड़ी पुरानी मांग चल रह� है �क इसको आप ब्रोडगेज लाइन बनाइएगा। कालका, जो ह�रयाणा \nम� है, इधर यह ऊना-तलवाड़ा लाइन बन रह� है, और हमार� जो बहुत पुरानी रे लवे लाइन है, उ स के \n�लए हमार� मांग है �क आप ब्रोडगेज लाइन के �लए इसका सव� करवा ल�िजएगा और जो�गन्दर नगर से \nआगे यह लाइन कु ल्लू, मनाल� तक जा सकती है, िजससे लोग� को ज्यादा फायदा �मलने वाला है। \nहमारे यहां जो कांगड़ा िजला है, जो कांगड़ा वैल� है, उसको टू �रज्म के �हसाब से और उद्योग के �हसाब \nसे आगे लाना है, इससे हमार� जनता क� आ�थर्क िस्थ�त सुधर सकती है। इस�लए इसक� तरफ भी आप \nज्यादा गौर क�िजएगा। हमारे यहां जो ऊना का स्टे शन है, उसम� शेल्टर नह�ं है। वहां लोग� को धूप, \nबा�रश म� ऐसे ह� बैठना पड़ता है। मेरा आपसे �नवेदन है �क आप इसक� तरफ भी ध्यान द�िजएगा। \n\n430 \nशताब्द� वगैरह दूसर� ट्रे न्स म� आपने सफाई का बहुत काम कराया है और यह काम सुचारू रूप से चल \nरहा है, ले�कन टॉयलेट्स क� तरफ थोड़ा सा �वशेष ध्यान दे ने के �लए आप अपने �वभाग के अ�धका�रय� \nको क�हए �क वे इस और जरूर ध्यान द�, िजससे �क और भी ज्यादा नीट और क्ल�न हो स के । \n\n431 \nमहोदय, म� आपका एक बार �फर धन्यवाद करती हूं, जो आपने �हमाचल के प्र�त अपना हाथ रखा \nहै, हम� भानुपल्ल� से �बलासपुर लाइन द� है, ले�कन जो दूसर� बात� म�ने आ प के सामने रखी ह�, उनक े \nऊपर भी आप गौर क�िजएगा। बहुत-बहुत धन्यवाद। जय-�हन्द। \nSHRI BIRENDRA PRASAD BAISHYA (Assam): Thank you Sir. I am thankful to \nyou for giving me this opportunity to speak on the Interim Railway Budget \npresented by the hon. Railway Minister, Shri Lalu Prasad Yadavji. Sir, in \nhis Budget Speech, the Railway Minister has announced Rs. 10,807 crores \nas Estimated Budget for implementation of the Report of Sixth Pay \nCommission, which will benefit lakhs of workers and officials of Indian \nRailways and funding of various on-going Railway projects of our country. \nSir, in his Budget Speech, the hon. Minister cat egorically said, proudly \nsaid that in the last five years Indian Railways' net profit is \napproximately Rs. 90,000 crores after decreasing the Railway fares, cost \nof Railway tickets in various classes of the Indian Railways. No doubt, \nthis is a great achievement of the Indian Railways and we must \ncongratulate the hon. Minister for his successful tenure. From the \nnational point of view, although the Budget is a good Budget, but, it is \nvery painful to say, Sir, that this Budget has totally neglected Assam \nand North-Eastern Region. This is a good Budget for other parts of the \ncountry. But, this is a bad Budget for the States like Assam and other \nNorth-Eastern States. I think, while preparing the Budget, the hon. \nRailway Minister might have forgotten Assam and the other North- Eastern \nregion. But, Sir, Assam is a part of India. There is no doubt that only a \nfew States are benefited from this Budget. Frankly speaking, due to this \nBudget, the regional imbalance among the States in our country is going \nto be increase. The Railway Ministry has totally failed to reduce \nregional imbalance in our country. \nSir, in his Budget Speech, the hon. Minister has announced various \nschemes, including the dream project of Bullet Train. Sir, bullet train \nis the most sophisticated super fast train of the world. It is running in \nFrance, Germany, Japan, etc. No doubt, it is a good move as all the \ndeveloped countries are using bullet train. I am ready to say that, on \nthe one hand, the hon. Minister is introducing bullet train and on, the \nother  there are no electrical lines in many parts of the country, there \nare no broad gauge lines, and there are no lines in various parts of \nAssam and the North- Eastern Region. Why is this discrimination? We have \nnothing to say against the introduction of bullet train. But, in the \nmeantime, the Government should seriously think that there should be \nelectrical rail line in Assam. There are no electrical rail lines in \n\n432 \nAssam. Can anybody imagine this? There is no broad gauge railway line. \nThere is no railway line in many parts of the North- Eastern Region. I \nhope the hon. Minister take this very seriously. Sir, in his speech, the \nhon. Minister said, 'Indian Railway Ministry, in the coming years, is \ngoing to introduce 42 new trains in our country.' It is good. But, among \nthese 42 new trains, not a single train is included for Assam or for any \nState of the North- Eastern Region! I hope I will get support from the \nHouse in this regard.  \nAnother important point, Sir, is, Assam is an insurgency- hit area. It \nis known to everybody. Unemployment is a big problem in our State. So, in \nthe last Budget Session, when I took part in the general discussion on \nthe Railway Budget, I categorically requested the hon. Minister to look \nafter this region and announce job reservation for local youth of the \nNorth-Eastern Region and Assam. In his Budget speech, the hon. Railway \nMinister has proposed to recruit 22,000 additional personnel for  \n\n433 \n3.00 P.M. \nthe Railway Protection Force and to create Battalions and Special \nProtection Force. So, I  would like to request the hon. Minister to \nprotect the interests of the people of Assam and the people of the North-\nEast Region by announcing that there will be 100 per cent reservation for \nthe local youth for the jobs in the North- Eastern Region. The Government \nshould announce a policy in this regard. \nWe also demand a coach factory in Assam. The Government is going to \nstart a coach factory in Kerala. It is, no doubt, a very welcome step. \nBut we-request that a coach factory should also be opened in Assam. It is \na long-pending demand of the people of Assam. \nIn the interest of the development of Assam and the North- East Region, \nwe request that a separate railway zone should be opened in the North-\nEast Region. It should be a separate railway zone, excluding Bihar and \nBengal. This railway zone in the North- East Region will, to some extent, \nalso solve the unemployment problem of the Region. \nAccording to a health survey, the maximum number of cancer patients \nbelong to Assam and the North-East Region. \nMR. DEPUTY CHAIRMAN: Conclude please. \nSHRI BIRENDRA PRASAD BAISHYA: Sir, please give me some more time \nbecause we have got nothing from the Railway Budget. I request you to \ngive me just a few more minutes. So, Sir, I was saying that, \"according \nto a health survey, the maximum number of cancer patients belong to Assam \nand the North- East Region. Every day, hundreds of cancer patients from \nAssam and from the North- East Region travel to Chennai and Mumbai for \nbetter medical treatment. But it is very difficult to travel to Chennai \nand Mumbai because there is only one train from Guwahati to Mumbai. It is \nalso not a regular train. So, we would like to request the hon. Minister \nto introduce a super fast train from Dubrigarh to Chennai and from \nDubrigarh to Mumbai. \nIn the year 1997, the then Prime Minister had laid the foundation \nstone of the Bogibeel Bridge in Assam. In the last Winter Session of \nParliament, in response to one of my questions, the hon. Railway Minister \nhad informed us that the Bogibeel Bridge would be completed by the year \n2012. \nMR. DEPUTY CHAIRMAN: You have taken a lot of time, Mr. Baishya. \nSHRI BIRENDRA PRASAD BAISHYA: But recently, the Railway officers told \n\n434 \nus that it is going to be completed by 2015. Sir, frankly speaking, the \nprogress in the construction of Bogibeel Bridge is very slow. It is so \nslow that out of 27 pillars, which are to be constructed there, not even \na single pillar has been constructed till date. \nMR. DEPUTY CHAIRMAN: Mr. Baishya, there are a number of speakers. I \ncan't give indefinite time to you. So, please conclude now. \nSHRI BIRENDRA PRASAD BAISHYA: Sir, I am concluding. Although the \nfoundation stone for this bridge was laid in 1997, not a single pillar \nhas been constructed as yet. This is due to lack of funds. When the \nIndian Railways is making a profit of more than Rs. 90,000/-  crores, and \nwhen it is going to  \n\n435 \nintroduce the bullet train in the country, why is Assam not getting money \nfor construction of a bridge? This is the sentiment of our people. I \nrequest the hon. Minister to understand our sentiment. Please try to \nunderstand the situation prevalent in Assam. \nI would request the hon. Railway Minister to develop the Guwahati \nRailway Station and to modernise it. This is the need of the hour. Sir, \nGuwahati is the hub of the North Eastern Region. There are seven sister \nStates, namely, Arunachal Pradesh, Assam, Meghalaya, Manipur, Mizoram, \nNagaland and Tripura. And, Guwahati is the hub of the North Eastern \nRegion. Being the hub of the North Eastern Region, it is the duty of the \nGovernment to modernise the Guwahati Railway Station. I hope he will look \ninto these issues and will, definitely, fulfil our demands. Thank you. \nसुश्री अनुसुइया उ इ के (मध्य प्रदे श): माननीय उपसभाप�त जी, आपने मुझे इस अंत�रम रे ल बजट \nपर बोलने के �लए जो समय �दया है, इ स के �लए म� आपको धन्यवाद दे ती हूं। माननीय मंत्री जी, \nआपने झांसी से �छन्दवाड़ा के �लए जो सुपरफास्ट ट्रे न चलाने क� घोषणा क� है, इ स के �लए म� आपको \nबहुत-बहुत धन्यवाद दे ती हूं। \nमाननीय उपसभाप�त जी, म� आ प के माध्यम से माननीय\n मंत्री जी का ध्यान इस ओर आक�षर्त \nकरना चाहूंगी �क �छन्दवाड़ा, �सवनी, बालाघाट तथा बैतूल, ये मध्य प्रदे श के आ�दवासी बाहुल्य �ेत्र ह� \nऔर इनम� बालाघाट, नक्सलवाद� ग�त�व�धय� से प्रभा�वत �ेत्र रहा है। वष� से यहां पर रे ल का \nआधु�नक�करण नह�ं हुआ है। साथ ह� �छन्दवाड़ा, �सवनी और बालाघाट िजल� म� वष� से नैरो गेज क� \nट्रे न� चलाई जा रह� ह�। \n[उपसभाध्य� (प्रो. पी.जे. कु �रयन) पीठासीन हुए] \nउपसभाध्य� महोदय, म� यहां पर बड़े दुख के साथ यह कहना चाहूंगी �क हमारे िजले म� एक \nउद्योग मंत्री जी ह�, िजन्ह�ने काफ� घ