घंटे  क�  रफ्तार  से  गाड़ी  \nचलने  क� कोई कल्पना नह�ं करता था। आप घड़ी और गाड़ी का  \n\n447 \nइम दोन� �मलाइए, साथ-साथ चल�गी। इस�लए सर, म� कहना चाहता हूं �क अगर कोई आसमान म� थूक \nफ� कता है, जलन से कोई थूक फ� के ग ा, तो वह थूक उस पर ह� पड़ने वाला है, �कसी दूसरे पर नह�ं \nपड़ेगा। सर, म� के व ल एक �मनट का समय और लेना चाहता हूं। 'अभी और भी काम बाक� है, अभी \nतो झांक� है और असल� काम बाक� है।' अभी लालू प्रसाद जी और भी काम करने वाले ह�। लालू प्रसाद \nजी को अगर दे श �मल गया, तो दे श म� भी कमाल कर�गे। ये कोई साधारण इंसान नह�ं है। ये एक ऐसे \nइंसान ह�, ऐसे फ�रश्ते ह�, िजन्ह�ने रे लवे क� पूर� तकद�र को बदलने का काम �कया है। इस�लए म� अंत \nम� आप से यह कहना चाहूंगा �क 'बढ़ गई है पीर पवर्त भी �पघलना चा�हए, इस �हमालय से कोई नई \nगंगा �नकलनी चा�हए, मेरे सीने म� न सह�, तेरे सीने म� सह�, हो कह�ं भी आग, ले�कन आग जलनी \nचा�हए'। \nTHE VICE-CHAIRMAN (PROF. P. J. KURIEN): Conclude please. \nश्री राजनी�त प्रसाद: म� लालू प्रसाद जी को �फर से धन्यवाद करता हूं, को�ट-को�ट धन्यवाद करता \nहूं �क जीयो हजार� साल, यह� तमन्ना, यह� आशा और यह� �वश्वास है। धन्यवाद। \nSHRI KUMAR DEEPAK DAS (Assam): Mr. Vice-Chairman, Sir, I would like to \nthank you for giving me the opportunity to participate in the discussion \non the Railway Budget. \nअभी-अभी मेरे का�बल दोस्त राजनी�त प्रसाद जी ने लालू प्रसाद जी के बारे म� काफ� बोला है। \nI also support it, and, I must congratulate Laluji. But, Sir, I would \nlike to mention something with regard to our State, our region. Sir, \nRailways has earned nearly Rs. 90,000 crore, but what we – the people of \nNorth-East, the people of Assam earn? In this Interim Budget, hon. \nRailway Minister has declared various factories in various parts of the \ncountry. But, he announced not even a single factory in the North East. \nWhat about Assam? After independence of 60 years, Assam has not got even \na single factory. The history of railway services in Assam and North East \nRegion is nothing but deprivation. The entire  region is still ill-\nconnected. The States of North East are yet to be connected by railway \nnetwork of India. ...(Interruptions)... \nTHE VICE- CHAIRMAN (PROF. P. J. KURIEN): Please, Mr. Madhu. \n...(Interruptions)... \nSHRI KUMAR DEEPAK DAS: There is no double track system. \n...(Interruptions)... \nTHE VICE-CHAIRMAN (PROF. P. J. KURIEN): Please ...(Interruptions)... \nSHRI KUMAR DEEPAK DAS: The gauge conversion work is moving at a \nsnail's pace. ...(Interruptions)... \nTHE VICE-CHAIRMAN (PROF. P. J. KURIEN): If you want to talk, talk in a \nvery low voice. \n\n448 \nSHRI KUMAR DEEPAK DAS: Even the scheduled dates of completion of \nvarious national projects are extended year after year, including the \nproject like Bogibill. It is unfortunate that the condition and amenities \nprovided in the long- distance trains from Delhi, Guwahati, Dibrugarh, \netc., are very poor. Dirty, dilapidated and deplorable coaches are being \nused which should have been discarded long back. Condition of the \nstations is pitiable. There is no connectivity of super fast trains \nbetween various important cities like Mumbai, Chennai, etc. Sir, railway \nauthorities have acquired enormous acres of land for its utility since \nlong back, but it is kept as it was. I would like to cite the  \nexample  of  Sorbhog where 400 bighas of land was acquired by the railway \nauthorities from the State  \n\n449 \nGovernment in early independence period but the same has been kept \nwithout any utility. Time and again, people have been demanding to take \nproject like coach manufacturing factory etc., but the authorities \nconcerned have done nothing so far. There is no facility of \nelectrification in railway track in this region whereas all the States of \nthe country are having the same. In comparison to railways total track \nregion of around 63,332 kilometers, only 2,400 kilometers fall in the \nNorth East Region, and 700 kilometers have been done by the Government of \nIndia.  On the one hand, 1,700 kilometers of railway in Assam was built \nby the British. I am sorry that except for gauge conversion, it largely \nremains a legacy of the British period. Indian Railways must change the \npresent attitude for the better development of the North East Region. \nSir, recently Tripura was connected by rail line. But it is meter gauge \nwhy? Why was it not connected by broad gauge? We are talking about Bullet \nTrain in other parts of the country and here we have constructed a rail \nline which is a meter gauge line. I would like to ask whether the Railway \nMinister will be able to show good gesture to spend one- fourth of the \nearnings of the railways for the development of the north East Region, \nfor improvement of the North East, for better economic development of the \nNorth East because we are already 30- 40 years behind in railway \ndevelopment in comparison to the entire country. Sir, I just want to \nmention about one question which I asked and which has been replied \ntoday. My question was: Whether the Government is aware that there is a \nlong standing demand for the construction of new railway line between \nGuwahati and Jogihopa via Barpeta-Hajo-Sualkuchi? The reply was, \n\"Available records do not indicate such demand\". Sir, I am sorry to say \nthat we are deprived not only of various projects but also of a simple \nassurance of development of railway in the North East Region. Sir, I \npersonally wrote a letter to the Minister and a number of times I have \nmentioned about these new Iines on the floor of this House but reply has \ncome that available records,do not indicate such demand. How has this \nhappened? What is the Railways doing? This type of deprivation should not \nbe there. I just request the hon. Railway Minister to look into the \ndevelopment of the railways in the North-East. Thank you. \nSHRIMATI T. RATNA BAI (Andhra Pradesh): Sir, I thank you for having \ngiven me this opportunity to speak on interim Railway Budget. \nSir, I regret to state that Andhra Pradesh, a fast- developing State, \nalways gets a raw deal. I don't know the reason behind it. \nSir, the Railways have not increased fares of the common man directly. \nBut the common man has to pay Rs.150 for sleeper class and Rs.300 for AC \nclass for their Tatkal tickets. It is clear that the hon. Minister has \nincreased the fares of common man in the form of Tatkal tickets \n\n450 \nindirectly. I request you to put a limit on the  tickets of Tatkal scheme \nto ease the burden of passengers. \nSir, the Railways are providing 20,000 extra special trains in the \nrush season. But the facilities in such special trains are not at the \nlevel of regular trains, because trains will be decided and run in the \nnick of moment, depending on the rush and demand of passengers. Water \nwill not be available in such special trains. Nobody knows the exact time \nof stoppage of special trains, because it affects the regular timings of \nregular trains. Regular trains are also running very late due to these \nspecial trains because of heavy traffic. Thus, the Railways are leaving \nthe safety of passengers in lurch. Hence, I request the hon. Minister of \nRailways to run full-scale trains when there is heavy rush and demand of \npassengers, especially to the South areas in the country with all \namenities. \n\n451 \nSir, there is every need to lay a new railway line for the route of \nManuguru-Kirandul and Manuguru-Bhadrachalam-Rajahmundry, because there is \nmuch demand from the people living in the vicinity of such areas which is \nbeneficial, especially for the scheduled agency areas in Andhra Pradesh. \nSir, it is a known fact that the Indian Railways is doing good job in \nterms of revenue earning over the last few years. The infrastructure of \nthe Railways also has been established to take care of the requirement of \nrailways. The Railways established the production units at various \nlocations in India, namely, the Rail Coach Factory, Kapurthala, the \nIntegral Coach Factory, Perambur, the Rail Wheel Factory, Bangalore, the \nDiesel Locomotive Works, Varanasi, the Diesel Component Works, Patiala, \nthe Chittaranjan Locomotive Works, Chittaranjan. Recently, one Wheel \nFactory has been established in Chabra, and one more Coach Factory was \nannounced in Kerala. But it is a lamented fact that Andhra Pradesh, the \nmain hub for railways movement, did not find any place for any of those \nfactories. \nIf you observe from what I have just said, there is no Wagon Building \nFactory established anywhere in India except at two locations, namely, \nMuzaffarpur and Mokameh in a small scale. Therefore, it is not out of \nplace to mention that one Wagon Building Unit can be established in \nAndhra Pradesh, in tribal Area for the development of tribal area. \nEstablishing the Wagon Building Unit not only just meet the urgent \nrequirement of the Railways, it is also helpful in the improvement and \ndevelopment of tribal Area of Andhra Pradesh. \nTHE VICE-CHAIRMAN (PROF. P. J. KURIEN): I can allow the rest to be \nlaid on the Table. \nSHRIMATI T. RATNA BAI: Sir, one more. Sir, Guntur is a very congested \nand important area in Andhra Pradesh. But it does not have proper railway \nfacilities. First a train will be introduced to Guntur only from other \ndestinations. But later the same train will be extended to other areas \nvia Guntur. Why are Railways not taking interest for developing the \nGuntur railway station? Sir, there is only one line from Secunderabad to \nGuntur via Nadikudi. This is really saving a lot of time and fare for the \npassengers. I am grateful for it. My request is to put a double line from \nSecunderabad to Guntur via Nadikudi. \nTHE VICE-CHAIRMAN (PROF. P. J. KURIEN): Now, please, Shrimati Ratna \nBai. \nरे ल मंत्री (श्री लालू प्रसाद): महोदय, मेरा आपसे अनुरोध है �क �ल�खत रूप म� दे दे ने से यह \nप्रोसी�ड ंग म� चला जाएगा और �रकॉडर् हो जाएगा। रे लवे बजट पर आज अं�तम �दन है, इ स के बाद हम� \n\n452 \nभी एक घंटा बोलना है। इस�लए अनुरोध है �क लोग �ल�खत रूप म� दे द�। उ स के ऊपर कायर्वाह� क� \nजाएगी। \nSHRIMATI T. RATNA BAI: Sir, because there is heavy rush in this route \nand sometimes, trains are stopped. If there is double line, the \npassengers can save a lot of time in reaching Guntur from Secunderabad \nwithout any hindrance via Nadikudi. Because there are hundreds of hamlets \nin the vicinity of Guntur area and most areas are scheduled agency areas. \nSir, I request the hon. Minister to give urgent importance to \nelectrify the rail route in the scheduled agency areas in Andhra Pradesh \nduring the current year without disturbing the afforestation on vacant \nrailway land, etc. \n\n453 \nSir, the railway accidents are familiar to the common man. This can be \navoided by adopting modern technologies especially in the scheduled \nagency routes of Railways in Andhra Pradesh. \nI request the hon. Minister to introduce Garib Raths from New Delhi to \nHyderabad and Visakhapatnam daily because of the heavy rush to these \nareas. \nSir, platform shelters are in a poor condition at smaller stations \nfrom protection against cold, heat and rain in most parts of Andhra \nPradesh especially in the remote areas and scheduled agency areas. This \nshould be improved immediately. \nThere is dire need of bullet train from Hyderabad to Vijayawada or \nGuntur for the convenience of passengers to save their time. I request \nyou to complete this project on a top priority. \nSir, I am happy to hear that a survey will be undertaken for \nPiduguralla-Narasaraopet route. Sir, I request you to undertake and \nextend such survey from Piduguralla- Narasaraopet-Chilakaluripet. From \nNarasaraopet to Chilakaluripet, the distance is only around 20 \nkilometres. And moreover, there are thousands of hamlets in the vicinity \nof Chilakaluripet and it also connects to the highway of Chennai route. \nThis will really be a boon for the people of Chilakaluripet if the \nrailway line is laid in this route. \nSir, I fully support this Budget and conclude my speech. Thank you, \nSir. \nSHRI TIRUCHI SIVA (Tamil Nadu): Sir, just restrict the time. Time \ncould be restricted. There may be those who want to speak. \n...(Interruptions)... \nTHE VICE-CHAIRMAN (PROF. P. J. KURIEN): Pardon me. What did you say? \nSHRI TIRUCHI SIVA: Sir, if it is a written copy, it can be laid. But, \nif  they want to speak, the time could be restricted so that they can \nconvey what they want within that stipulated time. We have been waiting \nfor the past two days. Sir, ten or fifteen minutes is not a problem. \nTHE VICE-CHAIRMAN (PROF. P.J. KURIEN): Okay. Let us restrict the time \nto five minutes each. There may be 6 or 7 speakers. Now, Shri Krishan Lai \nBalmiki. Only strict five minutes. \nश्री कृ ष्ण लाल बाल्मी�क (राजस्थान): धन्यवाद, उपाध्य� महोदय। म� रे लवे बजट पर बोलने के \n�लए खड़ा हुआ हूं। \nTHE VICE- CHAIRMAN (PROF. P. J. KURIEN): Have you got the written \nspeech? \n\n454 \nSHRI KRISHAN LAL BALMIKI: Yes, Sir. \nTHE VICE-CHAIRMAN (PROF. P. J. KURIEN): You can lay on the Table. \nSHRI KRISHAN LAL BALMIKI: Okay, Sir. \nमाननीय सदस्य: सर, माइक नह�ं है, कु छ नह�ं है, हम सब बोलने आते ह� तो टाइम नह�ं है। \nसर, यह क्या है। \nउपसभाध्य� (प्रो. पी.जे. कु �रयन): अभी आप बै�ठए। Mr. Balmiki, you speak and \nrestrict yourself to five minutes because you may be giving a lengthy \nspeech. We cannot allow that. Everybody, please, restrict yourself to \nfive minutes because we cannot lay it on the Table. We don't know what \nyou are giving. \n\n455 \nश्री कृ ष्ण लाल बािल्मक�: धन्यवाद, उपसभाध्य� महोदय। यह आरोप अपनी जगह पर सह� हो \nसकते ह� �क लालू जी क� पुरानी घोषणाएं अमल म� तब्द�ल नह�ं हो पातीं �क घोषणाओं क� अगल� \nफे ह � र स् त आ जाती है। यह मसला भी अपनी जगह बना हो सकता है �क राष्ट्र�य रे ल मंत्रालय एक हद \nतक �बहार रे ल मंत्रालय क� तरह काम करता है। बुलेट ट्रे न प�रयोजना क� शुरूआती रे ल �दल्ल� से पटना \nके बीच चलने क� संभावना है। �दल्ल�, अमृतसर, चेन्नई, ब�ग्लोर, दूसरे रूट ह�। �वप�ी पाट� भाजपा \nशा�सत गुजरात के �हस्से म� बुलेट ट्रे न नह�ं है। लेफ्ट के 