nterruptions)... \nश्री �वश्वजीत दै मार�: सर, यह बहुत जरूर� है। \nTHE VICE-CHAIRMAN (PROF. P. J. KURIEN): The rest you can write to the \nMinister. आपका पांच �मनट क� जगह छह �मनट \nहो गया। बाक� आप �लखकर मंत्री जी को दे \nद�िजए। \nश्री �वश्वजीत दै मार�: ठ�क है, म� �लखकर दे ता हूं। थ�क यू। \nउपसभाध्य� (प्रो. पी.जे. कु �रयन): मंत्री जी, बाक� यह �लखकर द�गे, आप कं स ी ड र क�िजएगा। \nश्री लालू प्रसाद: यह माननीय सदस्य कभी हमारे पास आते ह� नह�ं ह�। आप अगर वहां के �लए \nकं स न र् ह�, तो कभी आप आकर �मले ह� नह�ं ह�, आज ह� यहां बोल रहे ह�। ...(व्यवधान)... \nश्री �वश्वजीत दै मार�: एपायंटम�ट ह� नह�ं �मलता। \nउपसभाध्य� (प्रो. पी.जे. कु �रयन): आप �ल�खएगा। \nश्री लालू प्रसाद: कौन नह�ं दे ता है? हमारा �फक्स रहता है। \nश्री �वश्वजीत दै मार�: ठ�क है। \n\n460 \nश्री �गर�श कु मार सांगी (आंध्र प्रदे श): उपसभाध्य� महोदय, सबसे पहले म� खड़ा हो रहा हूं, लालू \nजी ने जो अंत�रम रे लवे बजट पेश �कया है, उ स के समथर्न म�। \nTHE VICE-CHAIRMAN (PROF. P. J. KURIEN): Thank you. Mr. Sanghi. Take \nonly five minutes. Please be very brief. \n\n461 \nSHRI GIREESH KUMAR SANGHI: Sir,  I will complete it in three minutes. \nTHE VICE-CHAIRMAN (PROF. P. J. KURIEN): Okay. Thank you. \nश्री �गर�श कु मार सांगी: सर, रे लवे मंत्री लालू प्रसाद यादव जी क�, यहां तकर�बन िजतने भी \nस्पीकसर् ने बात क� है, सबने तार�फ क� है, थोड़ा सा जरा हमारे आंध प्रदे श क� तरफ आप ज्यादा \nध्यान द�, तो म� उनका आभार� रहूंगा, क्य��क �पछले बजट म� भी आंध्र प्रदे श के �लए कु छ ज्यादा नह�ं \n�कया गया था। हम सभी मैम्बसर् ऑफ पा�लर्याम�ट उनसे जाकर �मले थे और आंध्र प्रदे श क� िजतनी भी \nसमस्याएं ह�, उनक े बारे म� हमने उनको बताया था। अगर हम� अपने दे श क� प्रग�त को एक्सीलेरेट करना \nहै, तो the Railways is the lifeline of development; the Railways is the \nindicator of development; the Railways accelerates the development. लाल ू \nप्रसाद जी के कं ध � पर इस दे श क� प्रग�त क� रफ्तर को आगे बढ़ाने क� और भी ज्यादा िजम्मेदार� है। \nआपने दे खा है �क हर एक स्पीकर ने उनक� इतनी तार�फ क� है और इस तार�फ से उनक� िजम्मेदार� \nऔर भी बढती है, यह नह�ं �क इससे उनम� कोई complacency आ जाए �क म� काम कर रहा हूं। \nउससे हमार� जो आशाएं ह�, जो टारगेट है, वह पूरा नह�ं होगा। म� आशा करता हूं �क िजस रफ्तार से \nइं�डयन रे लवे आगे बढ़ रहा है, आने वाले �दन� म� भी यह और प्रग�त करे और अच्छ�-अच्छ� ट्रे न� चालू \nकरे । \nहमारे आंध्र प्रदे श क� कु छ demands ह�, जो म� आ प के माध्यम से मंत्री जी को बताना चाहूंगा। \n�सक ं दराबाद-बीकानेर एक्सप्रेस, जो once in a week चलती है, इसको कम से कम तीन �दन प्र�त \nहफ्ता कर� तो बहुत अच्छा रहेगा। क्य��क हैदराबाद और इ स के आस-पास के शहर� म� राजस्थान के बहुत \nसारे लोग बसे हुए ह�। वे अपने तीथर्स्थल या अपने native place regular जाना चाहते ह�। Once \nin a week जो यह ट्रे न चलती है, उसम� बहुत लम्बी वे�टंग �लस्ट होती है, तो अगर वह इसको कम \nसे कम तीन �दन प्र�त हफ्ता कर� तो म� उनका बहुत आभार� रहूंगा। म� उनको धन्यवाद दे ता हूं �क जो \n�सक ं दराबाद-पटना एक्सप्रेस हफ्ते म� दो �दन चलती थी, उन्ह�ने उसे सात �दन �कया है। इससे बहुत \nराहत �मल� है। �बहार के कई लोग हैदराबाद और आस-पास के शहर� म� नौकर� करते ह�। खासकर बहुत \nसारे स्वणर्कार लोग हैदराबाद म� काम करते ह�। उनको इससे बहुत राहत �मल� है। यहां पर �सक ं दराबाद-\nराजकोट एक्सप्रेस क� भी बहुत ज्यादा �डमांड है। यह हफ्ते म� तीन �दन चलती है। इसको भी daily \n�कया जाए तो बहुत अच्छा रहेगा। जो हैदराबाद शहर है, वह आंध्र प्रदे श का कै � प ट ल है। यह पूरे साउथ \nम� और पूरे दे श म� बहुत जल्द� आगे बढ़ रहा है और तरक्क� कर रहा है। यह बहुत बड़े मेट्रो �सट� के \nरूप म� shape ले रहा है। अगर हम इसक� प्रग�त को और भी आगे बढ़ाना चाहते ह� तो मेरा लालू जी \nसे अनुरोध है �क यहां से Banglore, Chennai, Mumbai, Nagpur, Tirupati and Vaizag \nऔर आस-पास के िजतने भी शहर ह�, उनको कनैक्ट करते हुए अगर शताब्द� एक्सप्रेस चलाई जाए तो \nऔर भी अच्छा रहेगा। यहां क� एक जो मेजर �डमांड है - क्य��क आस-पास से immigration बहुत \nज्यादा होने के कारण हैदराबाद म� population का concentration बहुत ज्यादा हो रहा है \n...(समय क� घंट�)... तो अगर यहां से इंटर�सट� एक्सप्रेस और भी ज्यादा चलाई जाए, हैदराबाद के \nडेढ़-दो सौ �कलोमीटर दूर पर जैसे Nalgonda, Khammam, Warrangal and Karimpnagar और \nइसी तरह के कई शहर आस-पास ह�, उनम� अगर इंटर�सट� फास्ट ट्रे न्स चलाई जाएं तो बहुत अच्छा \nरहेगा। \nम� पुन: लालू जी को धन्यवाद दे ता हूं �क इन्ह�ने इतना अच्छा बजट पेश �कया है और यह लगातार \n\n462 \nपांच वष� से बजट पेश कर रहे ह� और रे लवे म� काफ� तरक्क� हो रह� है। हमारे हैदराबाद म� एक छोटा \nसा प्रॉब्लम है। ...(Time-bell rings)... I will complete in five minutes. Sir. \nTHE VICE-CHAIRMAN (PROF. P. J. KURIEN): Not five minutes more. Five \nminutes are already over. \n\n463 \nSHRI GIREESH KUMAR SANGHI: I will complete in five minutes, Sir. हैदराबाद \nम� एक मेजर समस्या है। हमारा जो inner ring road है , उसका expansion हो रहा है, \nwidening हो रहा है। वह inner ring road रे लवे क� प्रॉपट� के बीच म� जा रह� है िजससे \nwidening म� �दक्कत आ रह� है, उसको अगर लालू जी थोड़ा दे ख� तो अच्छा रहेगा। आप सबको \nमालूम है �क रे लवे �कतना important है और जो रोड ट्रै वल है - रोड ट्रै वल म� जो accidents होते \nह�, अगर हम उन accidents से बचना चाहते ह� ...(व्यवधान)... \nउपसभाध्य� (प्रो. पी.जे. कु �रयन): पांच �मनट हो गया। \nश्री �गर�श कु मार सांगी: नह�ं हुआ है सर। \nउपसभाध्य� (प्रो. पी.जे. कु �रयन): हो गया। \nश्री �गर�श कु मार सांगी: दे श म� हर साल एक लाख आदमी accidents म� मरते ह�। अगर हमार� \nरे लवे और improve हो और हम रोड ट्रांसपोटर् से रे लवे म� �शफ्ट ह� तो कई जान� बच सकती ह�। मेरा \nउनसे यह� अनुरोध है, बहुत-बहुत धन्यवाद। \nSHRI TIRUCHI SIVA : Mr. Vice- Chairman, Sir, the Railways is a much \nsought after mode of travel for comfort and safety at a cheaper cost. It \nis a well- known fact. Sir, I take this opportunity to congratulate and \nappreciate the hon. Minister of Railways, Shri Lalu Prasad Yadav for \nhaving engineered the train of the Indian Railways to achieve record \nprofits, maintaining, at the same time, the standard of service and \nefficiency, continuously for four years. Adoption of new technologies by \nthe Railways has increased the safety and security of the passengers \nalso. There may be one or to mishappenings, but at the same time, we \nshould agree that comparatively, it is much less than it was in the past. \nI do not need to take much time of the House. It is a well- known and \nestablished fact that after Laluji assumed office of the Railways, it is \nall for appreciations from all quarters. I wanted to say this while \nsumming up my speech. This time, I personally want to congratulate and \nthank him on behalf of my State, Tamil Nadu, for he has announced five \nnew trains and has also introduced two- three extension trains and he has \nconceded all the demands of our leader, the Chief Minister of Tamil Nadu, \nDr. Kalaignar. Personally, Sir, when I spoke on the Railway Budget last \ntime, I had demanded a daytime inter-city train from Trichy to \nTirunelvelii. Thanks to the hon. Railway Minister and the Minister of \nState, Shri R. Velu, for taking the initiative and now they have \nannounced introduction of a new train from Trichy to Madurai and Madurai \nto Trichy which will help all the people who go to the Madurai High \nCourt. Personally, we are very grateful to them. When we speak something \non the floor of the House during a debate, generally, it is being \nlistened to. But he has accommodated the recommendations of the Members \nof Parliament. He has reciprocated and conceded many of our demands. Even \n\n464 \nmy colleagues said that the extension of the Chennai- Nagore train would \nbe a boon to the Thiruvarur people, our leader's birthplace. \nSir, I want to bring one or two demands, especially, to the notice of \nthe Minister of State, Shri Veluji. We need a train from Mayiladuthuri to \nCoimbatore, and one daytime inter- city train from Trichy to Bangalore \nwhich will have a very good patronage and it will be well appreciated by \nall; so also a tri-weekly train from Madurai to Tirupathi, which has been \nsuggested by many people from all quarters. Laluji may not be accessible \nto the last man, but his train is accessible to the last man. It serves  \nevery  ordinary  poor person. I am very happy that this UPA Government \nand also the President in her  \n\n465 \nAddress has lauded to the higher most level, Laluji's performance in the \nRailways, especially, quoting the construction of a dedicated freight \ncorridor between Kolkata and Ludhiana on the Eastern route and Mumbai and \nDadri on the Western route to augment the capacity of carrying freight \ntraffic. He has won accolades from the President to the last citizen. I \nthank him once again. Moreover, I have one important demand. He is very \ncompassionate to the senior citizens and all the people, invariably. I \nthink he would concede this demand also. I request him, on behalf of the \nold-age parents of the Railway employees, that they should be treated as \ndependents of the family unit so that they can become eligible for \nmedical facilities and family free passes. This would not incur much \nexpenses for the Railways. At present, there are 10 categories of the \nRailway Family Unit. I will just quote one thing which is quite strange. \nTaking the parents of the Railway employees into the'family unit would \nnot cost the Railways much. In one category, it says: \"...the sons of \nrailway employees, over 21 years of age, without an upper age limit, even \nif not a student or invalid, provided he is wholly dependent on and \nresides with the railway employees.\" It goes on like that, and there you \nhave ten categories. Here, as I mentioned, including the aged parents of \nthe railway employees into the family unit will get you a very good name, \nand people will appreciate you, especially, in the present times, when \npeople are let down by their children themselves. All these things will \nadd feather to the cap of the UPA Government. \nI would like to say only one thing to the hon. Railway Minister. Some \nMembers criticised you; some did not appreciate what you have done. And, \nthere may be some demands which have not been fulfilled. I would like to \nquote a few lines from a Tamil poem: \n\"Potruvar potrattum; puzhudhi vaari thootruvaar thootrattum. \nEtradhoru karuthu enadhullam enruraithaal, evar varinum nillane, \nanjane.\" \nIt means, \"Whoever wants to praise us, let them praise. Whoever wants \nto abuse us, let them abuse. If my mind says that it is right, then, I \nwill march on. I won't be afraid of anybody. I won't stop for anybody \nbecause my goal is clear.\" That is the goal of Laluji, and that is the \ngoal of the UPA. Thank you, Sir. \nSHRI SYED AZEEZ PASHA (Andhra Pradesh): Sir, as the Representative of \nAndhra Pradesh, I want to convey the sentiments of the people of Andhra \nPradesh that they have got a very raw deal in the Railway Budget. Even \n\n466 \nthough a common proverb says, \"कर  मेहनत तो खा नेमत, मेहनत का फल ´ÖßšüÖ\", \nbut, here, in spite  of the efficiency, in spite of the revenue increase \nby the South-Central Railway, we have not got that type of a deal which \nthe people of Andhra Pradesh had expected. \nThe hon. Member, Shri Girish Sanghi has given some suggestions and I \nfully endorse his view. Shatabdi Express should be introduced linking \nHyderabad to various other important neighbouring cities. While coming to \nother problems, the Tatkal system, as many of my colleagues have also \nmentioned, should be rationalized properly. Presently, a person, starting \nhis journey from Delhi, wanting to get down at Nagpur or Hyderabad, is \ncharged up to Yeshwantpur, Bengaluru. I think this is irrational. So, it \nhas to be rationalized properly. \n\n467 \nAs regards internet booking of tickets, I think, the city code should \nbe simplified, as it is there in the U.S. and other countries. Most of \nthe time, while searching for stations on the internet, it becomes very \ndifficult. So, I feel that the Ministry should find a more simplified \nmethod. Then, I am sorry to say that there is not even a single toll free \nnumber for the Railways. I think it is the urgent need of the hour. \nSecondly, whenever any accident takes place, you divert the train from \none place to another. But the time limit is not properly adhered to. In \nsuch a situation, there is a delay of seven or eight hours also. In this \nsituation also, we have to adhere to the time table. Sir, what I would \nlike to say is that even though the efficiency of the Railways has \nincreased, yet, punctuality has become the casualty. For the past six \nmonths, I have travelled extensively to several places. Believe me, \nexcept at two or three places, 10 per cent of the trains reached at the \ncorrect time – 90 per cent of the trains reached their destinations late, \nranging from 30 minutes to even eight hours. This is my personal \nexperience. I do not know why Laluji is not in a position to make \npunctuality a strict code. That is my personal request. \nI have one more request to make on behalf of the people of Hyderabad. \nPeople, in great numbers, go to Ajmer Sharief Durgah. Just like we have \nthe Kaifiat Express in the name of Kaifi Azmi, if a train in the name of \nMaqdoom Mohiuddin, who was also a very great poet of India, could be \nintroduced from Kacheguda to Ajmer, either bi-weekly or tri-weekly, then, \nthe people of Hyderabad would feel highly thankful. \nThen, as per the Catering Policy, 2005, where 12 per cent licence fee \nis to be charged on the annual sales turnover, the IRCTC, at the time of \nfixing the licence fee, is not adhering to the norms and code. \nThen, I just wanted to remind that the Standing Committee on Railways \nin its Report of 2006- 07 has said that snacks and light refreshment \nshould be made available on no- profit-no-loss basis. The Standing \nCommittee had also attacked the new policy of commercialisation and \nprofiteering of this business. It had recommended that the Railways \nshould not exploit the food and snack business by making it a profit-\nmaking business and that the Railways should not leave its social \nobligation. Sir, this policy of commercialisation and profiteering has \nclearly endangered the livelihood of 24 lakh food vendors which will \naffect nearly 1.5 crore dependents who belong to the Dalits or \nminorities, women, OBCs and other categories. Even though Laluji had \nassured on the floor of Lok Sabha that he would protect the interests of \nthe Dalits and STs from the purview of the IRCTC, but it is not being \nimplemented. I just wanted to draw his attention this issue. \n\n468 \nFinally, I have gone through the Report of the Comptroller and Auditor \nGeneral for the year 2006- 07. They have pointed out so many serious \nlapses. If you look at this Report from Chapter 2 to 5, you will find a \nnet loss of Rs. 1630.67 crores. The Railway Minister should look into \nthis Report and try to rectify it so that profits can further be \nincreased. \nLastly, my colleague was just pointing out that Asansol is the 6th \nfastest growing city in India. The Railway Ministry should take this into \nconsideration and see to it that Rajdhani stops at Asansol and it also \ngets connected to various other cities. \nश्री मोहम्मद अल� खान (आन्ध्र प्रदे श): शु�क्रया, उपसभाध्य� महोदय। म� रे लवे बजट के ऊपर \nरे लवे के वजीर जनाब लालू प्रसाद साहब को मुबारकबाद दे ते हुए उनसे उम्मीद करता हूं, चूं�क �म�नस्टर \nपर काम  का बोझ ज्यादा  \n\n469 \nहोता है, इस�लए स्टे ट के साथ इंसाफ करने म� थोड़ी-बहुत कोताह� हो जाती है। म� आन्ध्र प्रदे श से \nनुमाइंदगी करता हूं। म� दो-तीन बात� को वजीरे मोसूफ़ क� नजर म� लाना चाहता हूं। हमारे मुख्यमंत्री ने \nवजीरे मोसूफ़ को मकतूब �लखकर यह कहा था �क गुंतकल म� जो कोच rahabilitation \nworkshop है, इसको वहां पर कायम �कया जाए। दूसर�, काझीपेट म� जो टाइम टू टाइम इलेक्ट्र�क\n \nइंजन के �लए repair centre रखा जाता है, उसको भी वहां पर कायम �कया जाए। \nउपसभाध्य� महोदय, म� आ प के तवस्सुत से वजीरे मोसूफ़ से एक गुजा�रश करता हूं �क आन्ध्र प्रदे श \nके �लए जो नई ट्रे न� ह�, िजसक� मंजूर� हुए दस साल से भी ज्यादा हो गया है, ले�कन finance क� \nवजह से  \nशायद इनका आगाज नह�ं हो पाया है। इस�लए म�, दरख्वास्त क रूं ग ा �क लालू प्रसाद जी इस \nतरफ \nतवज्जो  \nद� और आन्ध्र प्रदे श क� अवाम क� जो उमंग� ह�, उनको पूरा कर